/* Quiet Worlds: a year on each planet. Day 1 arrival, three choice beats, and the other ending (alt). ok = follows the planet's rule. */
window.QW_STORY = {"endless-evening":{"arrive":"The sun sits low and gold, and your little house hums along its rails. Behind you, the sky is a very dark blue.","beats":[{"day":40,"text":"The wheels have started to squeal. A small oil can hangs by the door, with a label in neat handwriting: Sundays.","options":[{"t":"Oil the wheels","ok":true,"r":"The squeal fades to a purr. The sunset looks a shade warmer."},{"t":"Let it squeal for now","ok":false,"r":"The house slows a little. Behind you, the blue turns closer to black."}]},{"day":150,"text":"You wonder what lies behind the house. Out the back window, frost is creeping up the glass, and the rails behind you glitter white.","options":[{"t":"Walk back to look","ok":false,"r":"Ten steps in, your breath freezes in the air. You run back to the warm porch."},{"t":"Draw the curtains","ok":true,"r":"You make tea and watch the gold side. The frost never reaches the front."},{"t":"Sit on the back step","ok":false,"r":"The cold bites your fingers. The house waits for you, patiently."}]},{"day":300,"text":"Sunday again, and the oil can is nearly empty. There is one more can on a high shelf, and a nap sounds lovely.","options":[{"t":"Climb up for the new can","ok":true,"r":"Fresh oil. The engine sighs happily and the house rolls on into the gold."},{"t":"Nap first, oil later","ok":false,"r":"You wake to silence. The house has stopped, and the dark is one field away."},{"t":"Use the last drops sparingly","ok":false,"r":"The wheels groan. You lose a little of the sunset to the dark."}]}],"alt":"Some Sundays you forgot, and the dark crept close enough to frost the windows. But the house kept rolling, and so did you."},
"candy":{"arrive":"The air smells of caramel and the gingerbread house is warm. On the sink sits a new toothbrush. The calendar says October 30th.","beats":[{"day":30,"text":"Caramel for every meal so far. Tonight a back tooth gives a tiny twinge, and the toothbrush on the sink is still bone dry.","options":[{"t":"Have one more caramel","ok":false,"r":"Delicious. The twinge is still there at breakfast, a little louder."},{"t":"Brush before bed","ok":true,"r":"Minty and clean. The twinge is gone by morning."},{"t":"Rinse with hot chocolate","ok":false,"r":"Lovely and warm. Your tooth does not agree."}]},{"day":140,"text":"The gingerbread folk invite you to a toffee feast that lasts all night. The calendar still says October 30th. It always will.","options":[{"t":"Go, toothbrush in your pocket","ok":true,"r":"You dance till late, then brush by the fountain. Your teeth sparkle."},{"t":"Go, and brush tomorrow","ok":false,"r":"The feast is wonderful. In the morning, your smile feels sticky."},{"t":"Nap in a toffee armchair","ok":false,"r":"You wake stuck to the chair, with something fuzzy on your teeth."}]},{"day":290,"text":"Your toothbrush is worn flat. The sweet shop sells a lovely sugar toothbrush. There is also a plain wooden one in a drawer, a bit scratchy.","options":[{"t":"Buy the sugar toothbrush","ok":false,"r":"It tastes wonderful. It does not clean anything at all."},{"t":"Keep using the flat one","ok":false,"r":"It mostly moves the caramel around."},{"t":"Use the scratchy wooden one","ok":true,"r":"Not much fun, but your teeth squeak clean."}]}],"alt":"You skipped a few brushes, and one tooth wobbled by December. But the caramel was worth it, mostly, and you came home smiling carefully."},
"snow-globe":{"arrive":"Snow drifts down, soft and never cold. The bakery smells of fresh bread, and the sky curves a little, like glass.","beats":[{"day":50,"text":"The baker waves up at the empty sky every morning, for no reason you can see. She catches you watching, and smiles.","options":[{"t":"Shrug and walk on","ok":false,"r":"The baker looks a little worried. A shadow slides over the glass."},{"t":"Wave up at the sky too","ok":true,"r":"Nothing happens. The baker gives you a warm roll for joining in."},{"t":"Pull your hood down low","ok":false,"r":"You feel watched all day, and a little rude about it."}]},{"day":180,"text":"At dusk a huge round shape fills the sky, and a giant eye blinks through the glass. The whole village waves and cheers.","options":[{"t":"Wave with both arms","ok":true,"r":"The eye crinkles happily and drifts away. The snow falls extra soft tonight."},{"t":"Run indoors and hide","ok":false,"r":"From the window you see the eye search the streets, a little sad."},{"t":"Stare back, very still","ok":false,"r":"The eye taps the glass gently. It only wanted a hello."}]},{"day":330,"text":"Shake day. The ground tilts, snow whirls upward and loaves tumble out of the bakery. Above, the giant eye is watching closely.","options":[{"t":"Shout at the sky to stop","ok":false,"r":"The shaking stops. The eye looks away, and the snow turns a little grey."},{"t":"Hide under the bakery table","ok":false,"r":"Bread rains down around you. When you peek out, the eye has gone."},{"t":"Hold on tight and wave","ok":true,"r":"You wave mid-tumble. The eye winks, and the world settles gently."}]}],"alt":"You forgot to wave a few times, and the sky felt a little lonely. But the bread was warm, and the snow kept falling softly."},
"hot-spring":{"arrive":"Steam curls off your hot spring and snow falls on the inn roof. On the fence, three red faces watch you with great interest.","beats":[{"day":30,"text":"Snow monkeys join you in the water each evening. One keeps staring at your wrist, where your watch glints in the lantern light.","options":[{"t":"Keep it on, it's waterproof","ok":false,"r":"A small hand darts out. Your watch is now on the fence, ticking proudly."},{"t":"Leave the watch in your room","ok":true,"r":"The monkey sighs and settles for a warm soak beside you."},{"t":"Show the monkey your watch","ok":false,"r":"It admires it very closely, then runs off with it."}]},{"day":150,"text":"In the inn's lost property box: two old spoons and a tarnished ring. The monkeys peer in at the window, eyes on anything that shines.","options":[{"t":"Give the monkeys the trinkets","ok":true,"r":"They wear them proudly all evening. Your own watch stays safe in its drawer."},{"t":"Wear your watch to show them","ok":false,"r":"They are very impressed. So impressed that they keep it."}]},{"day":300,"text":"Midwinter. A monkey offers you a pinecone and points at the broken old watch on your shelf. Your good one ticks in the drawer.","options":[{"t":"Trade it the broken watch","ok":true,"r":"The monkey wears it all winter, very proud. Your good one stays hidden."},{"t":"Wear your good one to soak","ok":false,"r":"It is gone before the second bubble."},{"t":"Leave the drawer open","ok":false,"r":"In the morning, the drawer is empty and the fence is ticking."}]}],"alt":"The monkeys got your good watch in the end, and wore it better than you did. You told the time by the steam all winter."},
"cloud-islands":{"arrive":"Your windmill turns slowly on a cloud the size of a garden. The orchard is heavy with apples, and there is no ground anywhere below.","beats":[{"day":25,"text":"Picking apples at the cloud's edge makes you dizzy. A note nailed to a tree says: Eyes on the apples, not the gap.","options":[{"t":"Peek over the edge","ok":false,"r":"The world tips. You sit down hard and hug the tree for a while."},{"t":"Keep your eyes on the apples","ok":true,"r":"The basket fills up. The wind hums happily round your ankles."},{"t":"Lie flat and look over","ok":false,"r":"It is a very long way down. You crawl home and sleep badly."}]},{"day":160,"text":"You slip off the edge. The wind catches you, warm and gentle, and starts lifting you home. Below is a very long way down.","options":[{"t":"Look up at the windmill","ok":true,"r":"The wind sets you down on the porch, with a leaf in your hair."},{"t":"Close your eyes and trust it","ok":true,"r":"A soft bump, and you are home. The wind seems to giggle."},{"t":"Look down to see how far","ok":false,"r":"Your stomach drops. The wind wobbles, then sighs and carries you anyway."}]},{"day":280,"text":"A rope bridge now joins your cloud to a new island full of cherries. The planks are thin, and between them there is only sky.","options":[{"t":"Count the planks as you step","ok":false,"r":"Between the planks there is nothing at all. Your knees turn to jelly."},{"t":"Walk, eyes on the cherries","ok":true,"r":"You reach the far side humming. The cherries are perfect."}]}],"alt":"You looked down more than you should, and some nights you dreamed of falling. But the wind always brought you home."},
"cat-village":{"arrive":"The sea is warm and the rent is one fish a week. A ginger cat is already sitting on your table, looking at your teacup.","beats":[{"day":20,"text":"You set your tea on the table to read. The ginger cat looks at the cup, then at you, and slowly lifts one paw.","options":[{"t":"Wave the cat away","ok":false,"r":"It hops down, offended, and swipes the cup off on its way."},{"t":"Keep reading, it won't dare","ok":false,"r":"It dares. Tea on the floor, and one very proud cat."},{"t":"Pick the cup up and hold it","ok":true,"r":"The cat sighs and curls up in your lap instead. Tea stays in the cup."}]},{"day":120,"text":"Forty cats come to visit and fill every chair. Your favourite mug sits on the shelf, right next to a swishing tail.","options":[{"t":"Hold your mug while you host","ok":true,"r":"They knock everything else off, delighted. Your mug survives."},{"t":"Leave it on the shelf","ok":false,"r":"Crash. Forty cats look at you with great satisfaction."},{"t":"Shoo them all outside","ok":false,"r":"One slips back in, sulking, and nudges your mug off the shelf."}]},{"day":260,"text":"You buy a new mug, the last one in the shop. It is tall and wobbly. At home, the cats sit in a row along the table edge.","options":[{"t":"Put it down for one second","ok":false,"r":"One second is plenty for a cat. The shop is out of mugs now."},{"t":"Drink with both hands on it","ok":true,"r":"Forty cats watch, defeated, then fall asleep in a big warm heap."}]}],"alt":"Your mugs kept ending up on the floor, and you drank a lot of tea from saucers. But forty cats purred you to sleep every night."},
"pillow-hills":{"arrive":"The quilt hills are soft and the night light glows amber. A glass of warm milk waits by your pillow. You feel sleepy already.","beats":[{"day":30,"text":"You wake from what felt like a short nap. Your milk has a skin on it, and dust lies on the night light. The old clock has no alarm set.","options":[{"t":"Roll over for five more minutes","ok":false,"r":"Five minutes turns into a week. The milk is very cold."},{"t":"Wind the clock, set an alarm","ok":true,"r":"It ticks gently. Tomorrow you will wake on time."},{"t":"Drink the milk, nap again","ok":false,"r":"Cold milk, deep sleep. A spider has moved into your slipper."}]},{"day":150,"text":"On the next quilt hill, a sleeper hasn't moved since you arrived. Cobwebs on her slippers. Your alarm rings, very loud.","options":[{"t":"Hit snooze, just once","ok":false,"r":"Once becomes many. Something spins a tiny web between your toes."},{"t":"Get up and stretch","ok":true,"r":"Your legs wobble, then wake. The hills look lovely from standing."},{"t":"Set an alarm for her too","ok":true,"r":"She stirs, blinks, and whispers thank you. Then she sets one for her neighbour."}]},{"day":290,"text":"Your loud alarm has broken. The shop sells a gentle bell alarm, or you could trust yourself to wake. The pillows feel extra soft today.","options":[{"t":"Trust yourself to wake","ok":false,"r":"You wake in what might be next spring. The milk has turned to cheese."},{"t":"Sleep in, just today","ok":false,"r":"Today becomes a month. Dust settles on your eyelashes."},{"t":"Buy the soft bell alarm","ok":true,"r":"It rings like a quiet morning. You wake every time."}]}],"alt":"You slept through more mornings than you meant to, and lost a month or two somewhere in the quilts. But you always woke up, eventually."},
"turtle-back":{"arrive":"The palm tree sways and the hammock rocks. Under you, the island breathes slowly. It is a turtle, and a very friendly one.","beats":[{"day":40,"text":"Words carved in the palm trunk: Ten minutes, once a year. Practise. Under them, someone has drawn a little smiling fish.","options":[{"t":"Practise in the shallows daily","ok":true,"r":"One minute, then two. Small fish nibble your toes, encouragingly."},{"t":"Nap in the hammock instead","ok":false,"r":"A lovely nap. The turtle rumbles underneath, as if reminding you."},{"t":"Float on top and sunbathe","ok":false,"r":"You float happily all spring, and never once go under."}]},{"day":170,"text":"The turtle's head dips under the waves for longer each day. One minute, then five. You can hold your breath for three.","options":[{"t":"Tie yourself to the palm","ok":false,"r":"The palm is very much part of the turtle. That won't help."},{"t":"Hope the dive is a short one","ok":false,"r":"The turtle's dips get longer, not shorter."},{"t":"Add a minute every week","ok":true,"r":"Four minutes, then six. You start to feel like a fish."}]},{"day":300,"text":"The turtle takes a huge, slow breath, as if getting ready. You can hold yours for nine minutes now, nearly ten.","options":[{"t":"Squeeze in one last practice","ok":true,"r":"You reach ten minutes just as the turtle tips forward. Perfect timing."},{"t":"Jump off and swim away","ok":false,"r":"The sea is very wide without the turtle. It circles back for you, worried."},{"t":"Breathe deep and hold on","ok":true,"r":"Ten minutes of glowing fish and blue light. You come up laughing."}]}],"alt":"You didn't practise as much as you should. The dive was ten very long minutes, and you came up gasping. But the glowing fish were worth it."},
"kappa-pond":{"arrive":"The pond is very still and the tea house smells of green tea. In the reeds, something with a dish on its head is watching you.","beats":[{"day":20,"text":"The kappa climbs out and stands on your path, dish full to the brim. An old sign on the tea house shows two figures bowing.","options":[{"t":"Hand him a cucumber","ok":false,"r":"He takes it and steps closer, dish still full, eyes on the rest."},{"t":"Bow to him, low and polite","ok":true,"r":"He bows back, spills his dish, and hurries off to refill it."},{"t":"Wave hello","ok":false,"r":"He does not wave back. He steps closer, dripping."}]},{"day":130,"text":"Fog on the pond. Wet footsteps follow you as you carry the tea tray. Behind you, water sloshes in a very full dish.","options":[{"t":"Hurry inside with the tea","ok":false,"r":"The footsteps follow you to the door, and wait there all night."},{"t":"Offer him a cup of tea","ok":false,"r":"He takes it, and his dish stays full. He watches you drink."},{"t":"Set down the tray and bow","ok":true,"r":"He bows back. Splash. Off he pads to the pond, embarrassed but polite."}]},{"day":280,"text":"A visitor asks how to greet the kappa. He is watching from the reeds, waiting to see who will move first.","options":[{"t":"Wait for him to bow first","ok":false,"r":"He waits too. It is a very long, very damp afternoon."},{"t":"Bow first, and show her how","ok":true,"r":"You both bow. He bows twice, spills twice, and leaves two cucumbers."}]}],"alt":"You forgot to bow a few times, and he followed you home dripping. But most mornings he bowed, spilled, and left a cucumber."},
"penguin-bay":{"arrive":"The ice shelf glitters and a thousand penguins shout hello. Your stone hut is warm. One small penguin is staring at you, holding something.","beats":[{"day":15,"text":"The small penguin waddles up and drops a smooth grey pebble at your feet. Then it waits, flippers out, very hopeful.","options":[{"t":"Toss it back on the beach","ok":false,"r":"The penguin stares at the pebble for a long time, then sits on it."},{"t":"Pretend you didn't see","ok":false,"r":"It nudges the pebble closer. Then closer again."},{"t":"Pick it up and say thank you","ok":true,"r":"The penguin does a little dance and toddles off, very pleased."}]},{"day":100,"text":"A pebble every day now, each smoother than the last. A note in your hut says: Here, a pebble is a promise. Today's is pink.","options":[{"t":"Add it to your pebble pile","ok":true,"r":"The penguin sees your pile and honks with joy."},{"t":"Give it to another penguin","ok":false,"r":"Your penguin turns its back. The other one looks very confused."},{"t":"Build it a pebble nest","ok":true,"r":"It climbs in, wiggles, and adds a pebble of its own."}]},{"day":250,"text":"A snowstorm. Your penguin is waiting at the door, a pebble in its beak, shivering a little.","options":[{"t":"Take the pebble, shut the door","ok":false,"r":"Half a yes. It peers through the window until dawn."},{"t":"Let it in by the fire","ok":true,"r":"It drops the pebble in your hand and falls asleep on your feet."},{"t":"Keep the door shut, it's cold","ok":false,"r":"In the morning the pebble sits on the step. The penguin sulks by the shore."}]}],"alt":"You turned down a pebble or two, and your penguin sulked for a week. But it kept coming back, and so did the pebbles."},
"hibernation":{"arrive":"The cave is warm and the bear's arm is softer than any bed. Snow falls outside. The bear rumbles in his sleep.","beats":[{"day":20,"text":"You talk in your sleep and wake yourself. The bear's eyes are shut, but he mumbles: Salmon? One big ear is turned your way.","options":[{"t":"Hold your breath, say nothing","ok":false,"r":"He mumbles again, louder, and starts to stir."},{"t":"Whisper: yes, salmon","ok":true,"r":"He smiles in his sleep and pulls you closer. Warm all night."},{"t":"Shout to wake him up","ok":false,"r":"A deep, grumpy growl. You lie very still until he snores again."}]},{"day":140,"text":"In his sleep the bear asks: Is the river frozen? A bat drops a pebble outside and the cave echoes. He hates noise.","options":[{"t":"Clap to scare off the bat","ok":false,"r":"The clap rings round the cave. His arm tightens, and he grumbles."},{"t":"Sing him a loud lullaby","ok":false,"r":"One eye opens. It is not a happy eye."},{"t":"Murmur: only on top","ok":true,"r":"He nods, still dreaming. The trout are safe underneath, he says."}]},{"day":300,"text":"The bear tells a long sleepy story about a fish that got away. It is very boring. You are very tired.","options":[{"t":"Ask him softly how big","ok":true,"r":"Very big, he whispers. You both fall asleep smiling."},{"t":"Roll away to the cold corner","ok":false,"r":"It is cold away from him. He calls for you in his sleep, louder."},{"t":"Groan and cover your ears","ok":false,"r":"He grumbles awake for a moment, then sleeps with his back to you."}]}],"alt":"Some nights you were too loud and he growled in his sleep. But he always pulled you back in, and told you about fish."},
"seal-bay":{"arrive":"The bay is sunny and the ice is blue. Your fishing hut has a bed, a stove, and a round wet nose pressed to the window.","beats":[{"day":10,"text":"Six in the morning: knock, knock, knock. A seal with a hopeful face. A note pinned inside the door says: Neil is family.","options":[{"t":"Pull the blanket over your head","ok":false,"r":"The knocking goes on until seven. Neil sounds very sad."},{"t":"Open up for Neil","ok":true,"r":"Neil flops in, eats your breakfast fish and naps in your bed. He is thrilled."},{"t":"Lock the door","ok":false,"r":"Neil sits outside all day, staring through the window."}]},{"day":120,"text":"Neil has stolen your fish again. The shop sells a strong door lock, and also a little flap for seals.","options":[{"t":"Fit the seal flap","ok":true,"r":"Neil goes in and out forty times. He is so proud."},{"t":"Fit the strong lock","ok":false,"r":"Click. At six, a slow, sad knock. Then nothing."},{"t":"Just leave the door open","ok":true,"r":"Neil wanders in with a fish of his own, as if to say sorry."}]},{"day":280,"text":"A storm is blowing in fast. The wind keeps trying to slam your door, and Neil is still out on the ice.","options":[{"t":"Shut it against the wind","ok":false,"r":"The storm howls all night. At six, a knock you can barely hear."},{"t":"Prop the door open and wait","ok":true,"r":"Neil skids in just before the snow, and sleeps on your feet all night."}]}],"alt":"Some mornings the door stayed shut, and Neil sulked out on the ice. But he always forgave you by lunch, and stole your fish anyway."},
"tiny-kaiju":{"arrive":"The meadow is sunny and your cottage is cosy. Next door, something very small stomps about and roars like a squeaky toy.","beats":[{"day":10,"text":"Each morning the kaiju flattens your cardboard city, then looks up at you, waiting. A box of tape and cardboard sits on your porch.","options":[{"t":"Hide the cardboard away","ok":false,"r":"It squeaks sadly and tries to stomp your shed instead."},{"t":"Build the city again","ok":true,"r":"It squeaks with joy and stomps it flat at once. Then it naps on your boot."},{"t":"Tell it to play elsewhere","ok":false,"r":"It stomps off and flattens your tulips, very slowly, looking at you."}]},{"day":120,"text":"You're tired of rebuilding. The kaiju sits on the flattened city, pouting, its little tail drooping in the dust.","options":[{"t":"Let it stomp the garden","ok":false,"r":"It stomps your carrots flat, still sulking."},{"t":"Build an even bigger city","ok":true,"r":"Towers, bridges, a cardboard castle. It roars its tiniest, happiest roar."},{"t":"Give it the tape to build","ok":false,"r":"It eats the tape. The city stays flat, and so does its mood."}]},{"day":260,"text":"This morning the kaiju sneezed, and a tiny puff of fire came out. It looks very surprised. The cardboard city is ready to be stomped.","options":[{"t":"Stop building, it's risky","ok":false,"r":"With nothing to stomp, it practises its fire on your fence."},{"t":"Give it a cool bath instead","ok":false,"r":"It squeaks, steams, then wanders off to puff fire at your hedge."},{"t":"Rebuild, with a bucket nearby","ok":true,"r":"It stomps and puffs, and you douse the flames. Your eyebrows are a bit shorter."}]}],"alt":"Some mornings you didn't rebuild, and the kaiju stomped your garden instead. You lost a fence and an eyebrow, but kept a friend."},
"panda-daycare":{"arrive":"The bamboo forest whispers and the cottage is sunny. Fifty fluffy babies tumble through the door. Each one is the size of an armchair.","beats":[{"day":20,"text":"The pandas ate the whole bamboo shed by noon. Now they're sitting on you, getting grumpy. The bamboo forest is a short walk away.","options":[{"t":"Offer them your sandwiches","ok":false,"r":"Gone in a second. Fifty hungry faces turn toward the cottage."},{"t":"Wait for them to doze off","ok":false,"r":"Pandas do not nap hungry. They sit on you harder."},{"t":"Go cut a huge pile of bamboo","ok":true,"r":"Fifty happy crunching sounds. They roll off you, one by one."}]},{"day":110,"text":"A note from the parents said: Back by dinner. That was weeks ago. The bamboo is growing back slowly, and the pandas want a picnic.","options":[{"t":"Pack a picnic of bamboo","ok":true,"r":"Fifty pandas roll down the hill after the basket. Nobody goes hungry."},{"t":"Ration it, half a stalk each","ok":false,"r":"Fifty sad sniffs. One climbs onto the cottage roof, which bends."},{"t":"Plant more bamboo by the door","ok":true,"r":"Green shoots by the week's end. The pandas guard them proudly."}]},{"day":290,"text":"Winter frost. The grove near the cottage is thin, and the pandas keep growing. High up the mountain, the bamboo is still thick and green.","options":[{"t":"Hope the parents come soon","ok":false,"r":"They don't. Fifty grumpy pandas sit in a circle around you."},{"t":"Climb up and cut a winter store","ok":true,"r":"A long, cold climb. The shed is full, and so are fifty round tummies."},{"t":"Feed them the vegetable patch","ok":false,"r":"They sniff the cabbages, unimpressed, and sit on the fence."}]}],"alt":"Some days the bamboo ran out and the pandas sat on you until it grew back. The parents came home in December to a very flat babysitter."},
"kitten-cottage":{"arrive":"Sunlight fills the cottage and the catnip garden hums. You sit down with one cup of tea, and the first kitten climbs into your lap.","beats":[{"day":20,"text":"Your lap is full of sleeping kittens. The kettle whistles across the room. Your neighbour once stood up fast, and still has the scratches.","options":[{"t":"Jump up for the kettle","ok":false,"r":"A hundred kittens wake at once, very offended. You collect a few scratches."},{"t":"Rise very, very slowly","ok":true,"r":"Kittens slide off like warm butter, still purring. You get your tea."},{"t":"Let the kettle whistle","ok":true,"r":"It whistles itself out. The kittens don't even twitch."}]},{"day":130,"text":"Four months and ten thousand kittens. Your legs are asleep, and a mouse squeaks outside. Every kitten's ear swivels.","options":[{"t":"Leap up to look outside","ok":false,"r":"Ten thousand kittens scramble at once. Your trousers will never be the same."},{"t":"Stamp to wake your legs","ok":false,"r":"The kittens bounce, startled, and dig in their claws to hold on."},{"t":"Stay still and stroke them","ok":true,"r":"The ears settle. A purr rolls across the room like a warm wave."}]},{"day":300,"text":"Spring. The kittens are bigger and heavier now. A friend knocks at the door, and every kitten is asleep on you.","options":[{"t":"Call out: come in, it's open","ok":true,"r":"Your friend tiptoes in and gets a kitten of their own. Very soft."},{"t":"Shoo them off quickly","ok":false,"r":"A grumpy flurry of fur. Someone bites your thumb, gently, on purpose."},{"t":"Stand up fast to answer","ok":false,"r":"Kittens everywhere, all cross. You open the door covered in tiny scratches."}]}],"alt":"You stood up too fast a few times, and wore the scratches all year. But ten thousand kittens forgave you, one purr at a time."},
"ice-fishing":{"arrive":"The lake is frozen blue and your little red hut is warm. You drop a line through the ice. Somewhere under there, something claps.","beats":[{"day":15,"text":"You catch a fat silver fish. A seal pops out of your fishing hole, looks at the fish, and claps its flippers hopefully.","options":[{"t":"Toss the fish to the seal","ok":true,"r":"It catches it mid-air and claps twice. You catch another straight away."},{"t":"Hide the fish in your coat","ok":false,"r":"The seal stares at you. Your line stays quiet the rest of the day."},{"t":"Shoo it back under the ice","ok":false,"r":"It sinks out of sight. The fish stop biting."}]},{"day":120,"text":"The seal is twice the size now. An old fisher by the shore says: Feed the lake, and the lake feeds you. Your bucket holds five fish.","options":[{"t":"Give it the smallest one","ok":false,"r":"It looks at the tiny fish, then at you. It does not clap."},{"t":"Share half the bucket","ok":true,"r":"Clap, clap, clap. Your line twitches again before you sit down."},{"t":"Tip in the whole bucket","ok":true,"r":"The seal does a delighted roll. Fish bite all afternoon."}]},{"day":280,"text":"A blizzard. One fish in all day. The seal looks thin and cold, and you're hungry too.","options":[{"t":"Save it for tomorrow","ok":false,"r":"The seal slips away. By morning, your hole has frozen over."},{"t":"Keep it, you need it more","ok":false,"r":"You eat alone. The ice is very quiet."},{"t":"Split the one fish","ok":true,"r":"Half each. Next morning, a fish waits on your doorstep, from the seal."}]}],"alt":"You kept a few fish for yourself, and the seal stopped clapping for a while. But it forgave you, and the fish kept biting."},
"duck-lake":{"arrive":"The lake is blue and the rowboat is red. A tiny duckling hatches by your porch, takes one look at you, and says: peep.","beats":[{"day":10,"text":"The duckling follows you everywhere. At night it sits by your bed and peeps, and peeps, until you pick it up.","options":[{"t":"Put it in a box by the door","ok":false,"r":"It peeps all night. In the morning, it looks at you sadly."},{"t":"Cuddle it to sleep","ok":true,"r":"It tucks its head under your chin and is asleep in a second."},{"t":"Take it back to the lake","ok":false,"r":"It waddles straight back to you, wet and confused."}]},{"day":120,"text":"Your duckling is the size of a large dog now. It still wants cuddles at bedtime, and you are busy fixing the boat.","options":[{"t":"Stop and cuddle","ok":true,"r":"It honks happily, then helps by sitting on the boat to hold it steady."},{"t":"Cuddle tomorrow instead","ok":false,"r":"It sulks by the water all night, and grows a bit grumpier."},{"t":"Give it some bread instead","ok":false,"r":"It eats the bread, then keeps staring at you, waiting."}]},{"day":220,"text":"Your duck is taller than the cabin. It wants to sit on your lap. You are not sure your lap will survive this.","options":[{"t":"Say no, it's too big now","ok":false,"r":"It tucks its huge head under one wing and won't look at you all day."},{"t":"Let it sit, gently","ok":true,"r":"It lowers itself very carefully. You are only a little flattened."},{"t":"Hug its neck instead","ok":true,"r":"It wraps its wings round you, warm as a quilt."}]}],"alt":"You skipped a few cuddles and the duck sulked for days. But it always came back to your lap, a little bigger every time."},
"manatee-bay":{"arrive":"Sunbeams fall through green water. A huge, soft manatee drifts up to you, whiskers twitching, and wraps its flippers around you.","beats":[{"day":10,"text":"The manatee hugs you every four hours, right on time. It is very heavy. A sign on the jetty says: Hug back. Not too hard.","options":[{"t":"Wriggle free and swim off","ok":false,"r":"It floats alone, blinking slowly, then follows you at a distance."},{"t":"Hug back, softly","ok":true,"r":"It hums a low, happy hum that you feel in your toes."},{"t":"Squeeze as hard as you can","ok":false,"r":"It squeaks and lets go, startled. The next hug is shy."}]},{"day":130,"text":"Two thousand hugs in, and your ribs ache. The four o'clock hug is due, and it's raining hard.","options":[{"t":"Skip it, just this once","ok":false,"r":"It waits by the jetty in the rain all night."},{"t":"Swim out for the hug anyway","ok":true,"r":"Warm sea, cold rain, one very happy manatee."}]},{"day":300,"text":"Your manatee arrives with a friend, even bigger. Both want a hug. Both are looking at you, whiskers twitching.","options":[{"t":"Hug both at once, tight","ok":false,"r":"Everyone squeaks. It is a lot of manatee all at once."},{"t":"Only hug your old friend","ok":false,"r":"The new one sinks to the sand, very sad."},{"t":"Hug one, then the other","ok":true,"r":"Two gentle hugs. Two very happy, very heavy friends."}]}],"alt":"You missed a few hugs, and your manatee drifted off to sulk. But it always came back, every four hours, give or take."},
"puppy-dorm":{"arrive":"The dorm room is cosy and the lamps are warm. A soft puppy sleeps in a dog bed by the radiator. A sign says No Pets Allowed.","beats":[{"day":10,"text":"Night. Something scratches at your door, small and patient. Your puppy wags at the door, then looks back at you.","options":[{"t":"Stuff a towel under the door","ok":false,"r":"The scratching goes on, muffled. Your puppy sleeps by the door, waiting."},{"t":"Open the door","ok":true,"r":"Five puppies tumble in, wagging. They take your bed. You take the dog bed."},{"t":"Point at the sign and sleep","ok":false,"r":"The scratching goes on until morning. Nobody sleeps much."}]},{"day":120,"text":"Two hundred puppies now. The night porter knocks: Any pets in there? Behind you, two hundred tails stop wagging.","options":[{"t":"Hide them in the wardrobe","ok":false,"r":"The wardrobe barks."},{"t":"Call through: no pets here","ok":false,"r":"The porter leaves. Two hundred puppies look at the door, unsure."},{"t":"Open up and smile","ok":true,"r":"The porter sees them, sighs, and comes back with a bag of biscuits."}]},{"day":280,"text":"Snow outside. The scratching at the door is louder than ever, with tiny shivering whimpers. Every bed in the room is full.","options":[{"t":"Open it anyway","ok":true,"r":"Twenty snowy puppies pile in. You all fit, somehow, in one warm heap."},{"t":"Leave it, there's no room","ok":false,"r":"The whimpers fade into the snow. You don't sleep well."}]}],"alt":"Some nights you kept the door shut, and the scratching kept you awake. But most nights you opened it, and slept warm under puppies."},
"rabbit-hills":{"arrive":"Wildflowers cover the hills and your carrot patch is neat. Two rabbits sit on the fence. You name the bigger one Steve.","beats":[{"day":30,"text":"Forty rabbits now. You try to name them all and get lost around Steve Twelve. Meanwhile, the carrot patch is looking thin.","options":[{"t":"Plant more carrots","ok":true,"r":"Fresh rows sprout. The Steves line up politely to wait."},{"t":"Start a list of names","ok":false,"r":"Steve Thirteen is also Steve Two. The carrots vanish while you write."},{"t":"Count the rabbits again","ok":false,"r":"You get forty-one, then fifty, then give up. No carrots left."}]},{"day":100,"text":"Four thousand rabbits. A notebook from the last tenant says: Don't count them. You'll never finish. Count what you can grow.","options":[{"t":"Call every one of them Steve","ok":true,"r":"It saves a lot of time. The Steves don't mind at all."},{"t":"Count rabbits one last time","ok":false,"r":"You reach nine hundred by sunset. Nobody had any dinner."},{"t":"Count carrots each morning","ok":true,"r":"Three hundred today. Enough for everyone, if they share."}]},{"day":260,"text":"The Steves have eaten every carrot. The village shop has a big sack of carrot seeds, or a thick book called Know Your Rabbits.","options":[{"t":"Buy the rabbit book","ok":false,"r":"It has six pages on faces. The Steves have four thousand of them."},{"t":"Buy the sack of seeds","ok":true,"r":"By midsummer, orange rows to the horizon. The Steves are delighted."}]}],"alt":"You spent too long counting rabbits, and some nights there were no carrots at all. But the Steves were good company, all of them."},
"endless-hotel":{"arrive":"The corridor goes on forever and your bed is very soft. A card on the pillow reads: Room service never closes. Doors open on three.","beats":[{"day":20,"text":"Three in the morning. Knock. Knock. Knock. Then a pause, long and careful, like something taking a breath.","options":[{"t":"Wait to see if it knocks again","ok":false,"r":"A fourth knock. Then a soft sound, from inside your wardrobe."},{"t":"Open the door now","ok":true,"r":"The hallway is empty. A tray of hot soup waits on the carpet."},{"t":"Hide under the blankets","ok":false,"r":"The fourth knock comes. In the morning, your shoes have moved."}]},{"day":150,"text":"You're in the bath at three when it starts. Knock. Knock. The door is right across the room, and you are dripping wet.","options":[{"t":"Shout: just a minute!","ok":false,"r":"The knocking pauses. Then a fourth knock, from the bathroom wall."},{"t":"Run for the door, dripping","ok":true,"r":"You open it on the third. Empty hallway, and a fresh towel on the floor."},{"t":"Finish your bath first","ok":false,"r":"Four knocks. When you come out, the bed has been turned down."}]},{"day":300,"text":"A note slides under your door: Room 413 waited to see who it was. Housekeeping found 413 very tidy. It is nearly three.","options":[{"t":"Look through the peephole","ok":false,"r":"Only darkness. While you look, it knocks a fourth time."},{"t":"Ask who it is first","ok":false,"r":"No answer. Just the fourth knock, very close."},{"t":"Stand by the door, hand ready","ok":true,"r":"Knock, knock, knock, and you open. Empty hall, extra soup."}]}],"alt":"You waited for the fourth knock one night too many. Room service still brings soup to your room, and leaves it on the carpet."},
"hedge-maze":{"arrive":"The fountain splashes and the kettle is always on. Around you, tall hedges stretch away to the edge of the world.","beats":[{"day":15,"text":"There's a brand new path in the hedges this morning. You're sure it was different yesterday. A note on the kettle: Every way leads here.","options":[{"t":"Mark the path with string","ok":false,"r":"The hedges grow overnight. In the morning, the string runs into a wall."},{"t":"Make tea and stay put","ok":true,"r":"Tea by the fountain. The roses open one by one."},{"t":"Follow the new path","ok":false,"r":"By dusk the hedge has closed behind you. You find the fountain at midnight."}]},{"day":120,"text":"A traveller stumbles into the middle, thin and dusty. She walked four months to find the way out, she says, and it came out here.","options":[{"t":"Try her route yourself","ok":false,"r":"The hedges shift by nightfall. You sleep in a cold dead end."},{"t":"Pour her a cup of tea","ok":true,"r":"She drinks three cups and laughs. She stays for the roses."}]},{"day":280,"text":"You're low on milk. The hedges have opened a long, straight path, and at the far end you can see something like a farm.","options":[{"t":"Walk to the farm for milk","ok":false,"r":"The path curls as you walk. The farm stays just ahead. Home at dawn, worn out."},{"t":"Drink your tea black","ok":true,"r":"Stronger than you like. The roses smell lovely anyway."},{"t":"Make rose-petal tea","ok":true,"r":"Pink and fragrant. You wonder why you ever wanted milk."}]}],"alt":"You went looking for the way out too often. The hedges closed around you, and the kettle in the middle whistled for nobody."},
"singing-swamp":{"arrive":"Warm night air, a gently rocking houseboat, and a million frogs singing. It is loud, and somehow very peaceful.","beats":[{"day":30,"text":"The frogs stop for ten seconds. Something heavy shifts in the water. In the houseboat log, in shaky writing: If they go quiet, be a frog.","options":[{"t":"Hold very still, silent","ok":false,"r":"The ripples drift closer to the boat before the frogs start again."},{"t":"Light the lantern to look","ok":false,"r":"In the silence, the light makes you easy to find. The ripples turn your way."},{"t":"Croak softly","ok":true,"r":"Your croak is awful. A frog nearby answers, and the song starts again."}]},{"day":160,"text":"The frogs stop mid-song. Far off, reeds bend one by one, as if something tall is walking. The swamp is completely silent.","options":[{"t":"Croak like a frog","ok":true,"r":"You sound very silly. The reeds stop bending, then turn away."},{"t":"Paddle away fast","ok":false,"r":"Your splashes ring out in the silence. The reeds bend toward you."},{"t":"Hide below deck","ok":false,"r":"Quiet in the dark. Something bumps the hull, slowly, twice."}]},{"day":320,"text":"Silence again, and this time it goes on and on. Your throat is dry. Something is breathing slowly, close to the bow.","options":[{"t":"Croak once, then wait","ok":false,"r":"One croak is not enough. The boat dips under a heavy weight."},{"t":"Keep croaking, however long","ok":true,"r":"Forty minutes of terrible croaking. Then, one by one, the frogs join in."},{"t":"Rest your voice a minute","ok":false,"r":"The breathing comes closer, and stops right beside you."}]}],"alt":"You went quiet when the frogs did. The next night the song began again, but one voice on the houseboat was missing."},
"rake-woods":{"arrive":"Pale moonlight between thin white trees. The cabin bed is the softest in the world. The door has a heavy bolt that sticks a little.","beats":[{"day":20,"text":"A hot night, and a breeze through the door would be lovely. On the porch, the boards creak under something you can't see.","options":[{"t":"Leave the door open a crack","ok":false,"r":"You wake at three. Something long and pale is sitting at the foot of your bed."},{"t":"Bolt the door and sleep","ok":true,"r":"It's warm, but you sleep deeply. Tall footprints on the porch at dawn."},{"t":"Drag the bed onto the porch","ok":false,"r":"Cool air, soft bed. Something very tall sits down beside you, and talks."}]},{"day":140,"text":"A voice whispers through the door. It knows your name, your grandmother's name, and where you lost your blue scarf.","options":[{"t":"Unbolt it, just to peek","ok":false,"r":"Long pale fingers curl round the edge, gently. It comes in to sit."},{"t":"Stay in bed, door shut","ok":true,"r":"The whispering is kind and patient. In the morning, your scarf is on the step."},{"t":"Open it to ask more","ok":false,"r":"It folds itself in, sits at the end of the bed, and tells you everything."}]},{"day":300,"text":"The bolt has rusted loose. The door rattles gently, and a soft voice asks: May I come in? Just to sit. I know things you'd like to know.","options":[{"t":"Say yes, just this once","ok":false,"r":"It ducks under the frame and sits. It talks until dawn, and you listen."},{"t":"Wedge a chair under the handle","ok":true,"r":"The door holds. The voice sighs, and tall, slow footsteps go back to the trees."}]}],"alt":"You opened the door too many times. By winter you never slept at all, only listened, and it never ran out of things to say."},
"gnome-garden":{"arrive":"The garden goes on forever, full of roses and smiling clay gnomes. The cottage is snug. The nearest gnome stands by the gate.","beats":[{"day":20,"text":"You slept a long nine hours. This morning the gate gnome is by the birdbath instead, still smiling, dew on its face.","options":[{"t":"Carry it back to the gate","ok":false,"r":"You put it back. You sleep well, and next morning it is nearer than before."},{"t":"Wake every two hours tonight","ok":true,"r":"Light, broken sleep. In the morning, not one gnome has moved."},{"t":"Sleep in, you're so tired","ok":false,"r":"The next morning, three gnomes are on the path, facing your door."}]},{"day":150,"text":"A gnome sits on the porch steps. The old gardener's diary ends: Slept all night at last. So comfy. A warm bath and bed are calling.","options":[{"t":"Wipe the dew off their faces","ok":true,"r":"They smile up at you, damp and patient. You nap in the chair after."},{"t":"Take a warm bath, then bed","ok":false,"r":"Wonderful sleep. One gnome is on the stairs, smiling."},{"t":"Doze in the hard armchair","ok":true,"r":"Light sleep, a creak or two. The porch gnome hasn't moved an inch."}]},{"day":300,"text":"A gnome is at the window, looking in. You haven't slept deeply in months. Tonight the bed looks so very soft.","options":[{"t":"Close the curtains and sleep","ok":false,"r":"Deep, dark sleep. In the morning, the curtain is open from the inside."},{"t":"Nap upright by the lamp","ok":true,"r":"You wake every hour. The gnome is still at the window, smiling, not moving."},{"t":"Sleep deeply, just once","ok":false,"r":"In the morning, a smiling gnome sits on the end of your bed."}]}],"alt":"One night you slept too deeply. In the morning the garden was full of smiling gnomes, and one of them looked a lot like you."},
"oasis":{"arrive":"Golden dunes, a warm night, a striped tent. Your camel nuzzles your shoulder. Far away, a lake shimmers on the sand.","beats":[{"day":30,"text":"You walk toward the shimmering lake. All morning it stays the same distance away. Your camel snorts and pulls back toward the tent.","options":[{"t":"Walk on, it must be close","ok":false,"r":"The lake vanishes at noon. Your waterskin is lighter than you'd like."},{"t":"Drink up, a lake is ahead","ok":false,"r":"Your skin is empty by the time the lake melts into sand."},{"t":"Turn back with the camel","ok":true,"r":"Home by dusk. The camel looks very pleased with itself."}]},{"day":140,"text":"An old map in the tent: Most lakes lie. Fill three skins. Turn back at half. You're packing for a long walk and want to travel light.","options":[{"t":"Fill all three skins","ok":true,"r":"Heavy, sloshing, slow. The camel carries two, grumbling."},{"t":"Take just one, to stay light","ok":false,"r":"Light and quick. By evening, you are very thirsty and very far out."},{"t":"Take two, that's plenty","ok":false,"r":"On day two you shake the last skin. It is nearly silent."}]},{"day":290,"text":"Two days out. Two lakes have vanished already, and a third glimmers ahead. You have water for one more day. Your camel stops.","options":[{"t":"Turn back for the tent","ok":true,"r":"You walk home. On the way the camel veers left, and finds a real pool."},{"t":"Just one more lake","ok":false,"r":"It shimmers, and it vanishes. The walk back is long and very dry."},{"t":"Follow where the camel goes","ok":true,"r":"It turns back the way you came, then sniffs out a pool behind a dune."}]}],"alt":"You walked one lake too far. Your camel came home alone, and it still waits by the striped tent every evening."},
"raptor-ferns":{"arrive":"The ferns are taller than houses, and your cabin stands on stilts. The lantern burns gold. In the ferns, three pairs of eyes catch the light.","beats":[{"day":20,"text":"The lantern oil is half gone. Five raptors watch from the ferns now. Their eyes follow the flame, not you.","options":[{"t":"Throw them some food","ok":false,"r":"They don't touch it. As the flame sinks low, they take a step closer."},{"t":"Blow it out to save oil","ok":false,"r":"In the dark, the ferns rustle closer. You relight it with shaking hands."},{"t":"Top up the lantern now","ok":true,"r":"The flame stands tall. Five pairs of eyes blink slowly, and stay put."}]},{"day":150,"text":"A storm. Rain hammers the roof and wind pushes through the shutters. Twelve raptors now, and the lantern flame shivers.","options":[{"t":"Shield it with your hands","ok":true,"r":"Your hands are warm all night. The flame never falters."},{"t":"Go to bed, it'll be fine","ok":false,"r":"You wake in the dark to a soft tapping on the stilts, all the way round."},{"t":"Latch the shutters tight","ok":true,"r":"The wind stays out. The flame steadies, and so do the eyes."}]},{"day":300,"text":"Forty raptors. They say this lantern never goes out, but the wick has burned to a stub. A spare wick sits in the drawer.","options":[{"t":"Trust it, it's never gone out","ok":false,"r":"At midnight it gutters. Forty shapes stand up in the ferns."},{"t":"Change the wick now","ok":true,"r":"The flame jumps bright. Forty pairs of eyes blink, and settle down."},{"t":"Change it in the morning","ok":false,"r":"Before dawn, the flame shrinks to a blue bead. The ferns go very quiet."}]}],"alt":"The lantern went out one night too many. In the morning the cabin on stilts stood empty, and the ferns were very still."},
"one-room":{"arrive":"One cosy room: a bed, a kettle and a window. This morning the window shows a pink desert. There is also a door.","beats":[{"day":30,"text":"Yesterday's door led to the same room: bed, kettle, window, another door. You came back. Today your window shows a snowy forest.","options":[{"t":"Go through again, and on","ok":false,"r":"Room after room, exactly the same. You are no longer sure which one was yours."},{"t":"Watch the snow with tea","ok":true,"r":"Snowflakes drift past. Your kettle is the only one you can hear."},{"t":"Lock the door, hide the key","ok":true,"r":"You tuck the key in the tea tin. The forest snows past your window all day."}]},{"day":160,"text":"From behind the door comes a sound: a kettle starting to whistle. You didn't put a kettle on. Yours is cold.","options":[{"t":"Press your ear to the door","ok":false,"r":"Footsteps. They stop on the other side, listening to you listen."},{"t":"Put your own kettle on","ok":true,"r":"Two kettles whistle, then only one. You drink your tea by the window."},{"t":"Open the door to see","ok":false,"r":"Another room. The kettle has just been lifted off. Nobody is there."}]},{"day":300,"text":"Tonight the handle of your door turns, slowly, from the other side. The window shows a calm grey sea.","options":[{"t":"Open it and say hello","ok":false,"r":"Nobody there. But a second cup sits by your kettle, still warm."},{"t":"Hold the door shut","ok":true,"r":"The handle turns, stops, and lets go. Next door, the kettle cools by night."}]}],"alt":"You opened one door too many. Someone else lives in your cosy room now, drinks tea by the window, and looks a little like you."},
"mirror-salt":{"arrive":"White salt to every horizon, a brick hut and a sack of rice. The lake is a perfect mirror. You wave, and your reflection waves, a little late.","beats":[{"day":30,"text":"Your reflection is always one second behind. Today it caught up, and moves exactly when you do. It looks pleased about it.","options":[{"t":"Kneel down to look closer","ok":false,"r":"It kneels too, nose to nose with you. Neither of you blinks."},{"t":"Look away and cook rice","ok":true,"r":"Steam and salt. When you glance back, it is a second late again."},{"t":"Test it with a little dance","ok":false,"r":"It dances perfectly in time. A little too perfectly."}]},{"day":170,"text":"Your reflection raises its hand. You haven't moved. It beckons, gently, toward the middle of the lake.","options":[{"t":"Walk where it points","ok":false,"r":"Out in the middle the salt is thin, and the reflection smiles wider."},{"t":"Copy its wave","ok":false,"r":"It waves, you wave. Soon you can't remember who started."},{"t":"Turn your back on it","ok":true,"r":"When you look again, it stands still, a second late as usual."}]},{"day":320,"text":"You wake to see your reflection in the hut window already up, walking to the door. It looks back, waiting for you to follow.","options":[{"t":"Hang the rice sack on the window","ok":true,"r":"No mirror, no hurry. By lunch, it is late again."},{"t":"Follow it outside","ok":false,"r":"It walks ahead, and you walk after. It never once looks back again."},{"t":"Stay in bed, eyes shut","ok":true,"r":"When you open them, it is back to being late. Rice for breakfast."}]}],"alt":"You followed it one time too many. Your reflection lives in the brick hut now, eating rice, and it is never late."},
"sheep-hills":{"arrive":"A green hill without end, a stone cottage and a hundred woolly sheep. The barn has a big iron lock, hanging open.","beats":[{"day":30,"text":"You count the sheep into the barn. Ninety-nine, one hundred, one hundred and one. You count again, and get a hundred.","options":[{"t":"Leave it open, it's peaceful","ok":false,"r":"In the morning, a sheep stands on your doorstep, staring."},{"t":"Lock the barn and go in","ok":true,"r":"Click. A quiet night. In the morning, a hundred sheep, exactly."},{"t":"Go in and count again","ok":false,"r":"At the back, a sheep stares at you without blinking. You leave quickly."}]},{"day":140,"text":"The extra one stands at the back of the barn and never blinks. The other sheep leave a wide gap around it. Night is falling.","options":[{"t":"Stare back to see who blinks","ok":false,"r":"You blink first. It takes one step closer."},{"t":"Lead it out of the barn","ok":false,"r":"It follows you, very close, all the way to your cottage door."},{"t":"Lock up as usual","ok":true,"r":"The lock clicks. Inside the barn, nothing makes a sound."}]},{"day":300,"text":"The lock is rusty and stiff, it's freezing out, and bed is warm. The barn door creaks in the wind.","options":[{"t":"Tie it shut with string","ok":false,"r":"In the morning, the string is on your doorstep, neatly coiled."},{"t":"Fight the lock until it clicks","ok":true,"r":"Click. In the morning the extra one stands outside, patient."},{"t":"Leave it, just for tonight","ok":false,"r":"You hear soft hooves on the path, coming toward the cottage."}]}],"alt":"You left the barn open one night too many. In the morning there were a hundred sheep, an empty cottage, and something sitting by the fire."},
"aurora":{"arrive":"The cabin is warm and Biscuit is already asleep on your feet. Outside, the aurora ripples green over the snow.","beats":[{"day":40,"text":"Biscuit loves the cold. Tonight he scratches at the door to go out, and the aurora is the usual green.","options":[{"t":"Let Biscuit out","ok":true,"r":"He rolls in the snow, then comes back in with frost on his nose."},{"t":"Keep the door shut tonight","ok":true,"r":"Biscuit sighs and flops by the stove. Nothing happens, and that is fine."},{"t":"Walk out alone under the lights","ok":false,"r":"The snow is very quiet. You come back colder than you meant to."}]},{"day":150,"text":"The aurora turns a deep red. Something scratches at the door, and whines just like Biscuit. Biscuit is asleep beside you.","options":[{"t":"Open the door a crack","ok":false,"r":"Something pale moves away from the gap. The scratching starts again, closer."},{"t":"Stay with Biscuit","ok":true,"r":"You keep a hand on his warm side. The scratching stops at dawn."},{"t":"Call out his name","ok":false,"r":"The scratching answers, in a voice very like a bark."}]},{"day":300,"text":"A long red night. The scratching comes back, and now Biscuit is not by the stove. You did not see him go out.","options":[{"t":"Open the door for him","ok":false,"r":"The cold rushes in, and it is not Biscuit on the step."},{"t":"Look under the bed first","ok":true,"r":"Biscuit is under the bed, shaking. You both stay very still until the green returns."}]}],"alt":"You opened the door one red night too many. In the morning, Biscuit sat by the stove alone, waiting for someone to come home."},
"paper-hills":{"arrive":"Paper hills fold away into the distance and paper birds flutter overhead. Your little house rustles in the breeze. The sky is clear, as always.","beats":[{"day":40,"text":"A paper bird lands on your hand. One wing has a dark, soft spot, and it's damp. Far away, a grey cloud sits on the hills.","options":[{"t":"Walk out to see the cloud","ok":false,"r":"The air grows heavy as you go. Your fingertips start to curl."},{"t":"Dry the bird and forget it","ok":false,"r":"The bird flies off happily. Tomorrow the cloud is a little closer."},{"t":"Start hunting for an umbrella","ok":true,"r":"Nobody has one. Nobody has needed one for a thousand years. You keep looking."}]},{"day":150,"text":"The cloud is bigger now. In the paper library you find two books: How to Fold an Umbrella, and A History of Sunshine.","options":[{"t":"Fold a paper boat instead","ok":false,"r":"It's a lovely boat. It will not keep you dry."},{"t":"Read the umbrella book","ok":true,"r":"Fold, crease, wax with a candle stub. By evening, you have an umbrella."},{"t":"Read about sunshine","ok":false,"r":"Lovely pictures. Outside, a single drop lands on your roof with a soft pat."}]},{"day":300,"text":"Rain begins, gently. You hold your waxed paper umbrella. Your neighbour has none, and is running for home.","options":[{"t":"Catch a raindrop in your hand","ok":false,"r":"The drop goes straight through your palm, leaving a small soft hole."},{"t":"Run for the house","ok":false,"r":"It's further than you thought. You arrive very soft around the edges."},{"t":"Share your umbrella","ok":true,"r":"You squeeze under it together. Your sleeve gets soggy, nothing else."}]}],"alt":"You never got your umbrella ready in time. The rain came softly, and in the morning the paper hills were a little flatter."},
"two-minute-world":{"arrive":"A planet so small you can see it curve away. Two minutes all the way round. Your footsteps echo oddly, as if from the other side.","beats":[{"day":30,"text":"You stop to tie your shoe. Far round the curve, footsteps carry on for a moment, then stop too.","options":[{"t":"Wait to see who comes","ok":false,"r":"The footsteps start again, coming round the curve, in no hurry."},{"t":"Walk on, tie it later","ok":true,"r":"Your lace flaps, but the far footsteps fall back into step with yours."},{"t":"Shout hello round the curve","ok":false,"r":"Silence. Then the footsteps start again, faster than yours."}]},{"day":150,"text":"You're tired. A bench sits by the path, with words carved in the seat: Never rest here. Somewhere behind you, footsteps.","options":[{"t":"Keep walking, slow and steady","ok":true,"r":"Your legs ache, but the footsteps behind keep their distance."},{"t":"Sit for just one minute","ok":false,"r":"The footsteps don't stop. They get louder, and you're up and running."},{"t":"Turn round to look","ok":false,"r":"Nothing behind you. But now the footsteps sound like they're ahead."}]},{"day":300,"text":"You nearly dozed off mid-step and slowed right down. Round the curve, the other footsteps are quicker now, and closer.","options":[{"t":"Stop and face them","ok":false,"r":"The footsteps slow, very near. You never see who, but you feel them there."},{"t":"Pick up your pace","ok":true,"r":"Left, right, left. The footsteps fall back to the far side, where they belong."},{"t":"Turn and walk the other way","ok":false,"r":"Now you are walking toward each other. The curve is very short."}]}],"alt":"One night you stopped walking, and the footsteps did not. Someone else walks the little planet now, keeping a careful pace."},
"upward-rain":{"arrive":"A warm cottage and a neat vegetable garden. Rain rises gently out of the soil into the sky. Your hat tries to go with it.","beats":[{"day":25,"text":"A carrot pops out of the soil and drifts slowly upward. It is just above your head. You could jump and catch it.","options":[{"t":"Jump for the carrot","ok":false,"r":"Your feet leave the grass. You grab the fence post just in time."},{"t":"Wave it goodbye","ok":true,"r":"It drifts up, waving its leaves. You plant another."},{"t":"Tie the rest down with string","ok":true,"r":"Each carrot gets a little lead. They bob in the wind, but stay."}]},{"day":140,"text":"A clear night. Far above drift a teapot, a shoe and a bicycle. One of them is waving. There's a puddle on the path to the shed.","options":[{"t":"Hop over the puddle","ok":false,"r":"Your heels lift a little too far. You land with a gasp."},{"t":"Splash straight through it","ok":true,"r":"Wet socks, but both feet stay firmly on the ground."},{"t":"Leap it with a run-up","ok":false,"r":"For a long moment you don't come down. Then, slowly, you do."}]},{"day":300,"text":"Hay fever season. A huge sneeze is coming, and your big sneezes always make you hop. Your heavy boots are by the door.","options":[{"t":"Grab the doorframe and hold","ok":true,"r":"Achoo! You hold on tight. Nothing leaves the ground but a dandelion."},{"t":"Sneeze and hope for the best","ok":false,"r":"Your feet lift. The fence post saves you, just."},{"t":"Pull on the heavy boots","ok":true,"r":"Achoo! You wobble, but the boots keep you down."}]}],"alt":"You jumped once too often. On clear nights now, something small waves down from the sky above the cottage."},
"ice-cream-truck":{"arrive":"A sunny street that never ends, a porch swing, and sprinklers ticking. Somewhere far off, a tinny little tune starts, then stops.","beats":[{"day":20,"text":"Ten to nine, and the sky is gold. Far down the street, a jingly song starts up. No children come out. Every porch light is on.","options":[{"t":"Run out to buy one","ok":false,"r":"Nobody is driving. The song slows as you reach it, and you run back, heart thumping."},{"t":"Go inside now","ok":true,"r":"The song passes your house and fades away. Hot cocoa instead."},{"t":"Wait on the swing to watch","ok":false,"r":"It rolls by slowly with nobody driving. The song slows down as it nears you."}]},{"day":150,"text":"You've never seen your neighbour. A note on her door: In by nine. Always. You're watering the roses, and it's quarter to nine.","options":[{"t":"Drop the hose and go in","ok":true,"r":"The sprinkler runs all night. The roses don't mind, and neither do you."},{"t":"Water until the song starts","ok":false,"r":"The song starts nearer than you thought. You reach the door with seconds to spare."},{"t":"Finish the roses quickly","ok":true,"r":"Done at ten to. You're inside with the door locked before the first note."}]},{"day":300,"text":"Ten to nine. Your cat is in the garden and won't come in. The song has started, and tonight it is slower and longer.","options":[{"t":"Call it from the porch","ok":false,"r":"The cat ignores you. The song gets closer, and slower, and closer."},{"t":"Wait for it to wander in","ok":false,"r":"The truck's headlights sweep the hedge. The song is nearly over."},{"t":"Scoop it up and run inside","ok":true,"r":"Door shut at nine on the dot. The song ends, a little disappointed."}]}],"alt":"You stayed out past nine one night too many. Now the ice cream truck has someone at the wheel, and it waves to your porch each night."},
"space-station":{"arrive":"The blue planet turns below, and the garden smells of tomatoes. The sun rises for the third time today. The radio crackles.","beats":[{"day":25,"text":"The radio counts in a calm voice: five, four, three, two. Then silence. It feels like it is waiting for you to finish.","options":[{"t":"Finish the countdown for it","ok":false,"r":"The radio crackles happily. Every light on the station dims, just for a moment."},{"t":"Turn it down and garden","ok":true,"r":"The silence goes on. Your tomatoes are coming along nicely."},{"t":"Ask it: two, then what?","ok":false,"r":"The radio hums, very interested, and asks you the same question back."}]},{"day":150,"text":"You count tomatoes out loud: four, three, two... and there is a single one left on the vine. The radio has gone very quiet.","options":[{"t":"Call it the last tomato","ok":true,"r":"The radio sighs and goes back to static. A lovely tomato."},{"t":"Count it out loud","ok":false,"r":"The radio clicks on. Somewhere on the station, something starts to hum."},{"t":"Count it silently","ok":true,"r":"Silence in your mouth, silence on the radio. Tomato salad tonight."}]},{"day":310,"text":"A message on the screen: Station check. Crew on board? Please say the number aloud. The radio is listening.","options":[{"t":"Read the number out loud","ok":false,"r":"The radio says, very softly: thank you. The garden lights go out."},{"t":"Say: just me","ok":true,"r":"The screen blinks and accepts it. The radio waits all night, then goes quiet."}]}],"alt":"One day you said it without thinking. The radio said thank you, and the lights went out one by one, very politely."},
"kelp-forest":{"arrive":"Warm gold water, swaying kelp, and silver fish that nudge snacks into your hand. The kelp leans in a little whenever you drift.","beats":[{"day":30,"text":"A fish brings you a mussel. The kelp never bothers the darting fish, but it has wrapped itself snugly around a sunken log that never moves.","options":[{"t":"Eat it on the move","ok":true,"r":"You munch and paddle. The kelp sways politely out of your way."},{"t":"Float still and enjoy it","ok":false,"r":"A frond curls round your ankle. You kick free, heart thumping."},{"t":"Rest on the sunken log","ok":false,"r":"The kelp tightens round the log, and you. You wriggle out just in time."}]},{"day":120,"text":"You are so tired. A note in a bottle, from a diver long gone: I learned to sleep in slow circles. Never, ever float.","options":[{"t":"Float on your back to nap","ok":false,"r":"You wake with kelp across your chest, holding on very gently. You swim off fast."},{"t":"Practise sleeping in circles","ok":true,"r":"You drift off mid-stroke, circling. You wake to fish, not fronds."},{"t":"Wedge yourself between rocks","ok":false,"r":"The kelp finds you in the night. By morning a green ribbon is tied round your wrist."}]},{"day":200,"text":"Day two hundred. Your nose itches terribly. Behind you the kelp sways closer, waiting, the way it waits beside the log.","options":[{"t":"Stop and scratch, just once","ok":false,"r":"One second. Something green settles round your neck like a scarf."},{"t":"Stop and sneeze it out","ok":false,"r":"The kelp hugs you mid-sneeze. You tear free, minus a sleeve."},{"t":"Rub it on your shoulder","ok":true,"r":"You scratch without missing a stroke. The kelp sighs and sways back."}]}],"alt":"You stopped one time too many. The kelp tucked you in like a quilt, and the silver fish still bring supper to the spot."},
"bunker-town":{"arrive":"Red roofs, gulls, and a steel hatch in your kitchen floor. Every house has the same hatch, and the same big scorch marks.","beats":[{"day":20,"text":"Sunday morning. The church bell rings three times and every neighbour vanishes down their hatch. The sea is very calm, and very blue.","options":[{"t":"Climb down and lock the hatch","ok":true,"r":"Thuds and roars all afternoon. You play cards by lamplight. The house holds."},{"t":"Watch from the window","ok":false,"r":"Something huge steps over the lighthouse. A roof tile lands in your sink."},{"t":"Finish breakfast first","ok":false,"r":"The windows rattle as you dive for the hatch, toast still in hand."}]},{"day":140,"text":"The roaring stops at noon. Quiet. A gull taps at the window upstairs. Your neighbour's note says: they always come back for round two.","options":[{"t":"Pop up for some fresh air","ok":false,"r":"A shadow slides over the kitchen. You tumble back down the ladder."},{"t":"Crack the hatch to listen","ok":false,"r":"Grit rains down the ladder. Something outside sniffs at the gap."},{"t":"Stay down until Monday","ok":true,"r":"At four the roaring starts again, right overhead. By Monday, all is calm."}]},{"day":280,"text":"This Sunday, only one kaiju walks out of the sea. There is no fight. It wanders up your street, sniffing roofs, looking for something.","options":[{"t":"Run for the hills","ok":false,"r":"It turns its great head and follows you, curious, all the way."},{"t":"Stay down, very quiet","ok":true,"r":"Sniffing at the roof all day. Then a huge sneeze, and footsteps going away."},{"t":"Peek up to see where it is","ok":false,"r":"An eye as big as your door looks in. It blinks, interested."}]}],"alt":"You peeked out one Sunday too many. The lonely kaiju picked up your house like a shell and carried it, and you, into the sea."},
"what-you-eat":{"arrive":"Apples on every branch, fat rabbits in the clover, a river full of fish. Every animal here looks a bit mixed up. A rabbit by the river has fins.","beats":[{"day":25,"text":"Since your first night of rabbit stew, your ears have grown long and soft. The deer here eat only apples, and look perfectly normal. Supper time.","options":[{"t":"Grill a fish from the river","ok":false,"r":"Delicious. By morning you can breathe underwater, a little."},{"t":"Pick a basket of apples","ok":true,"r":"Crisp and sweet. Your ears stop growing, at least."},{"t":"Try the wild mushrooms","ok":false,"r":"You wake up spotty, red and white, and oddly fond of damp places."}]},{"day":130,"text":"A neighbour with a very red, very floppy comb invites you to a feast: roast chicken, honey cakes, and a big bowl of apples.","options":[{"t":"Fill up on the apples","ok":true,"r":"You eat apples and chat. The neighbour clucks happily. Literally."},{"t":"Try a little of the chicken","ok":false,"r":"That night you sleep on one leg, and wake at dawn crowing."},{"t":"Have a honey cake","ok":false,"r":"Sweet and sticky. Bees follow you home, very interested in you."}]},{"day":260,"text":"Apples only now. Small leaves sprout in your hair, and a bird tried to land on you. Winter is coming and the trees are nearly bare.","options":[{"t":"Store the last apples","ok":true,"r":"You ration them all winter. The leaves in your hair turn gold and stay put."},{"t":"Fish through the ice","ok":false,"r":"Gills again. You spend the winter wishing you lived in the river."},{"t":"Share the bird's berries","ok":false,"r":"You wake with a feather or two, and a strong urge to fly south."}]}],"alt":"You ate a bit of everything. By winter you had ears, gills and feathers, and you hopped off into the forest, forgetting your own name."},
"blizzard-cabin":{"arrive":"Pines, a stove, and a thick rope tied from your back door to the woodshed. A tag on the knot says: one hundred steps.","beats":[{"day":30,"text":"The blizzard comes every night like clockwork. You need wood. The rope is stiff with cold, and the shed seems so close in the porch light.","options":[{"t":"Walk out holding the rope","ok":true,"r":"A hundred steps there, a hundred back. The stove roars all night."},{"t":"Dash out, it's not far","ok":false,"r":"Ten steps in, the porch light vanishes. You find the rope again by luck."}]},{"day":150,"text":"Halfway to the woodshed, you drop a mitten. It lies just out of reach, a dark spot in the white. Your bare hand is getting very cold.","options":[{"t":"Let go and grab it quickly","ok":false,"r":"You grab it and turn, and the rope isn't there. It takes a long minute to find."},{"t":"Leave it and keep going","ok":true,"r":"Your hand stings all night, but you are home. The mitten is gone by morning."},{"t":"Hook it with your boot","ok":true,"r":"You drag it close and never loosen your grip. Warm fingers all the way back."}]},{"day":300,"text":"Tonight the rope is a hundred and one steps. At step fifty it twitches. Someone up ahead is holding the other end, and says your name.","options":[{"t":"Stop and say hello","ok":false,"r":"It says hello back, in your voice. The rope tugs, gently, the wrong way."},{"t":"Let go and step aside","ok":false,"r":"The rope slides off into the white. You crawl home by the stove's glow."},{"t":"Keep holding, keep counting","ok":true,"r":"You pass something tall in the snow without looking. Step one hundred. The shed."}]}],"alt":"You let go of the rope one white night too many. The woodshed was a hundred steps away, and you walked a hundred and one."},
"slime-hills":{"arrive":"Rainbow hills, warm squishy ground, and a house on tall stilts. The stilts look a little shorter than in the picture.","beats":[{"day":20,"text":"You stop to admire the view and your boots sink to the ankles in pink. The neighbours are always strolling, even while they eat.","options":[{"t":"Stand still for a photo","ok":false,"r":"By the time it's taken you're shin deep. It takes ages to wiggle out."},{"t":"Walk while you look","ok":true,"r":"You pace in slow loops. The view is even nicer on the move."},{"t":"Sit down for a picnic","ok":false,"r":"The ground hugs you to the waist. A neighbour tugs you out, still walking."}]},{"day":140,"text":"Blue patches are spreading. A pebble you dropped on blue vanished in a blink. On pink, the same pebble took all afternoon.","options":[{"t":"Wait for the blue to turn pink","ok":false,"r":"The blue spreads under you while you wait. You leap free, minus a boot."},{"t":"Test it with one foot","ok":false,"r":"Your leg sinks to the knee in a second. It comes out with a loud slurp."},{"t":"Cross it at a run","ok":true,"r":"Your feet barely touch it. Blue sinks fast, but you are faster."}]},{"day":290,"text":"You wake at dawn and the house has dropped again. The ground under the stilts has turned deep blue. The next roof over is still pink.","options":[{"t":"Climb out and keep moving","ok":true,"r":"You hop to the next roof and walk on. Behind you, the house gives a soft gulp."},{"t":"Stay in bed till it passes","ok":false,"r":"The floor tilts. You jump out the window just before the blue reaches the sill."},{"t":"Pack your things first","ok":false,"r":"Each minute packing, the house sinks lower. You leave with half a suitcase."}]}],"alt":"You stood still a few times too many. The blue ground folded over you, soft and warm as a beanbag, and the hills grew a little taller."},
"boulder-giants":{"arrive":"Red rocks, warm pools, and giants who kneel so you can climb up. You count the rocks around your tent: six hundred, exactly.","beats":[{"day":30,"text":"A long walk, and your legs ache. A smooth, round, oddly warm rock sits by the path, perfect for sitting. A giant across the pool is watching.","options":[{"t":"Sit on the grass instead","ok":true,"r":"Soft and dry. The giant across the pool looks away, relieved."},{"t":"Sit on the warm rock","ok":false,"r":"The rock sighs under you. Across the pool, the giant stands up."},{"t":"Lean on it for a moment","ok":false,"r":"It shuffles away an inch. Big footsteps start coming closer."}]},{"day":150,"text":"A giant gives you a ride, and three small round rocks roll after her like ducklings. At the pool, she sets you down right beside them.","options":[{"t":"Pat a little rock hello","ok":false,"r":"It squeaks. The giant's huge head turns slowly toward you."},{"t":"Sit down among them","ok":false,"r":"The little rocks huddle and grumble. The giant lifts you away, not gently."},{"t":"Step back and give them room","ok":true,"r":"The giant rumbles softly, like a thank you. She gives you a ride home."}]},{"day":300,"text":"Back at your tent you count again: six hundred and one. The new rock is warm, right by your door, and shaped like a perfect stool.","options":[{"t":"Sit on your camp chair","ok":true,"r":"You drink your tea on the chair. The new rock shuffles closer, curious, then rolls off."},{"t":"Try out the new stool","ok":false,"r":"It is warm, and it purrs. The ground shakes as something big comes looking."},{"t":"Move your tent away","ok":true,"r":"You camp by the pool. The warm rock follows a while, then loses interest."}]}],"alt":"You sat on rocks once too often. One was a baby, and its mother carried you off, very carefully, to live in the far red hills."},
"frozen-lake":{"arrive":"The lake is frozen clear as glass, and the cabin smells of pine. You can see a long, long way down.","beats":[{"day":40,"text":"While you skate, shapes far below the ice seem to turn and follow you. They look like people, looking up.","options":[{"t":"Skate closer to look","ok":false,"r":"They rise a little to meet you. You decide you have skated enough."},{"t":"Skate near the shore only","ok":true,"r":"The shapes lose interest. You have a lovely afternoon by the reeds."}]},{"day":150,"text":"At night, a soft knock comes from under the cabin floor. Three knocks. Then, patiently, three more.","options":[{"t":"Knock back","ok":false,"r":"The knocking gets happier. It goes on until morning."},{"t":"Move your bed to the hill hut","ok":true,"r":"Up on the hill, the nights are silent. You sleep well."},{"t":"Put your ear to the floor","ok":false,"r":"Something on the other side does the same."}]},{"day":300,"text":"Late March. The ice groans and the knocking is everywhere now. An old sign at the shore says: Spring comes in April. So do they.","options":[{"t":"Stay for one last skate","ok":false,"r":"The ice is beautiful today. Under it, everyone is waiting."},{"t":"Pack up and leave the lake","ok":true,"r":"You walk inland on the last day of March. Behind you, the ice sighs."},{"t":"Board up the cabin and wait","ok":false,"r":"The boards are thick. The knocking is patient."}]}],"alt":"You left the shore on the last day of March. In April the lake thawed, and something waved after you from the water."},
"hourglass":{"arrive":"Warm dunes curl up the glass walls, and the sky shines through. Sand trickles down the middle like a slow, soft waterfall.","beats":[{"day":40,"text":"Each morning a fresh drift of sand covers the porch. A broom hangs by the door, worn smooth, with a little notch cut for every day.","options":[{"t":"Sweep it and cut a notch","ok":true,"r":"The porch is clean and bright. The house sits a little higher for it."},{"t":"Build a sandcastle on it","ok":false,"r":"A lovely castle. By morning the sand has swallowed your bottom step."},{"t":"Let the wind take it","ok":false,"r":"By evening the sand reaches the doorstep. The house settles, slightly."}]},{"day":160,"text":"The sand in the middle runs faster now. On quiet nights, from under the glass floor, you hear it: swish, swish. Someone else sweeping.","options":[{"t":"Tap on the glass floor","ok":false,"r":"The sweeping stops. Then a tap answers, right under your feet."},{"t":"Sweep your porch, then sleep","ok":true,"r":"Swish, swish, above and below. It is oddly comforting."},{"t":"Dig down to have a look","ok":false,"r":"The sand slides in faster than you dig. The porch is buried till noon."}]},{"day":330,"text":"The sand waterfall is nearly done. The dunes slide toward the middle, and your house slides with them. The broom is down to its last bristles.","options":[{"t":"Rest, it's nearly over","ok":false,"r":"You nap, and the house slides a whole metre toward the middle."},{"t":"Brush it clean by hand","ok":true,"r":"Grain by grain, the porch shines. The house holds its place."},{"t":"Climb the glass to the top","ok":false,"r":"The glass is smooth. You slide back down onto an unswept porch."}]}],"alt":"On the last day the glass turned over. Your swept porch came up on top, in the light. Far below, someone sighed, and started sweeping."},
"dog-park":{"arrive":"Sunny hills, a little house, and dogs everywhere, tails wagging. Each one sits by a garden gate, watching the path.","beats":[{"day":30,"text":"A spotty dog nudges your hand. Its collar says: If found, bring home. A gate number is scratched underneath, just over the hill.","options":[{"t":"Give it a biscuit and a pat","ok":false,"r":"It eats the biscuit and goes back to its gate, still watching the path."},{"t":"Walk it there right now","ok":true,"r":"At the gate it barks once and trots through. The latch clicks, happily."},{"t":"Take it there tomorrow","ok":false,"r":"It waits by your door all night, very politely. Its tail wags a bit less."}]},{"day":150,"text":"More dogs are waiting than you can walk in a day. An old dog by the pond has waited the longest. His collar is worn smooth.","options":[{"t":"Walk the old dog first","ok":true,"r":"He leans on you all the way. At his gate he looks back once, then goes in."},{"t":"Take the quick puppies first","ok":false,"r":"The puppies tumble home. The old dog lies down by the pond, still watching."},{"t":"Rest, and start tomorrow","ok":false,"r":"Tomorrow, every dog is still waiting, each a little greyer at the nose."}]},{"day":300,"text":"A scruffy dog follows you everywhere. Its collar says: If found, bring home. Under that, in faded letters, is your own address.","options":[{"t":"Ask it to wait right here","ok":false,"r":"It sits at once, and waits, and waits. You notice you are waiting too."},{"t":"Find it a gate in the park","ok":false,"r":"It won't go in. It sits at your feet, looking at the path out."},{"t":"Follow it to your own gate","ok":true,"r":"It trots ahead, checking you're still there. The path leads out of the park."}]}],"alt":"You never made them wait. On the last day a scruffy dog walked you to your own gate, and through it, and you were both home."},
"quiet-hospital":{"arrive":"Sunlight, a made bed, and fresh flowers by the window. Far down the hall, a heart monitor beeps, slow and steady, like a clock.","beats":[{"day":30,"text":"A card in the flowers says: come home. As you read it, the beeping down the hall quickens, just a little. Then it slows again.","options":[{"t":"Read it aloud, twice","ok":true,"r":"The beeping picks up, bright and quick. The flowers seem to lean toward you."},{"t":"Tuck it in the drawer","ok":false,"r":"The beeping slows. The hall feels a little longer than before."},{"t":"Nap in the sunny bed","ok":false,"r":"You sleep a long, soft time. The beeps are further apart when you wake."}]},{"day":160,"text":"The beeping is fainter. You follow it down the hall to a door you never noticed. Beyond it, someone is humming a song you know.","options":[{"t":"Go back to your quiet room","ok":false,"r":"The room is lovely and still. Down the hall, a beep goes missing."},{"t":"Hum along at the door","ok":true,"r":"The beeping steadies to the tune. The humming gets happier, and louder."},{"t":"Wait for a nurse to explain","ok":false,"r":"Nobody comes. The beeping waits, then slows, patiently."}]},{"day":320,"text":"The beeping is very slow now. A new card says: come home, we're right here. The bed has never felt softer. The hall door is open.","options":[{"t":"Rest a little longer","ok":false,"r":"The bed is so soft. The beeps come further and further apart."},{"t":"Rearrange the flowers","ok":false,"r":"They look lovely. Down the hall, the beeping pauses, then remembers."},{"t":"Walk out through the door","ok":true,"r":"With each step the beeping grows faster and stronger. The light ahead is warm."}]}],"alt":"The beeping grew strong and steady. One morning you opened your eyes in a different room, full of people saying your name. You were home."},
"lantern-lake":{"arrive":"Dusk, a still lake, lanterns floating like slow stars. A boat crosses, and everyone aboard waves at you, like family at a station.","beats":[{"day":30,"text":"The boat comes again at dusk, the passengers beaming at you. Last night you stayed indoors, and they waved a little less.","options":[{"t":"Watch from the window","ok":false,"r":"They wave at the dark window, then slowly lower their hands."},{"t":"Row out to meet them","ok":false,"r":"The boatman raises a hand. Not yet, he says. You turn back, chilled."},{"t":"Wave back from the jetty","ok":true,"r":"They light up and wave even harder. The boatman nods: not yet."}]},{"day":150,"text":"They wave most when you wave back with a lantern held high. One waves just like your grandmother did, with both hands, laughing.","options":[{"t":"Light a lantern and wave","ok":true,"r":"The lake brightens. Both her hands go up, and the whole boat cheers."},{"t":"Go to bed early tonight","ok":false,"r":"In the morning the jetty is damp, and the lake is very still."},{"t":"Ask to come aboard","ok":false,"r":"Not yet, he says. A few hands on the boat drop to their laps."}]},{"day":310,"text":"Winter. The boat is late, and the passengers look tired, hands drooping. The boatman watches the shore. A cold wind blows out your lantern.","options":[{"t":"Wait inside for the wind","ok":false,"r":"From the window you see the hands go down, one by one."},{"t":"Relight it and wave again","ok":true,"r":"Hands lift all along the boat. The boatman turns it around: not yet."},{"t":"Walk down to the boat","ok":false,"r":"There is a space on the bench, just your size. You step back, quickly."}]}],"alt":"You waved back every night of the year. On the last one the boatman smiled, said: not yet, not for years, and rowed away."},
"mushroom":{"arrive":"Soft moss, warm rain, and mushrooms glowing by the door, ready for supper. In the grass, a neat ring of them circles your house.","beats":[{"day":30,"text":"The ring mushrooms are fatter and glow brighter than the ones by the door. Moths that land on the ring never fly off. They just glow.","options":[{"t":"Pick from the ring","ok":false,"r":"Delicious. Your fingertips glow faintly until morning."},{"t":"Kick one out of the way","ok":false,"r":"Your toes tingle and glow. By morning it is back, a step closer."},{"t":"Pick the small ones by the door","ok":true,"r":"A simple supper. Outside, the ring glows on its own, untouched."}]},{"day":150,"text":"The ring is half as wide now, a step closer each night. Tonight it lies across the path to the stream, and you need water.","options":[{"t":"Hop over it, toes high","ok":true,"r":"You clear it with room to spare. The mushrooms lean after you."},{"t":"Push through, it's only fungus","ok":false,"r":"Spores puff up your sleeves. Your wrist glows all week."},{"t":"Catch rain in a bucket","ok":true,"r":"Warm rain fills the bucket by noon. You never go near the ring."}]},{"day":320,"text":"The ring reached the door last night. Thirty mushrooms, shoulder to shoulder, glowing on the step. The back window is still clear.","options":[{"t":"Sweep them off the step","ok":false,"r":"The broom glows, then your hands. The ring hums, pleased."},{"t":"Climb out the window and leap","ok":true,"r":"You land in soft moss, past the ring. Thirty caps turn to watch you go."},{"t":"Wait inside for it to move","ok":false,"r":"In the night the ring steps in. Your floor glows green by morning."}]}],"alt":"You never touched the ring. In autumn you leapt clear of it from the window sill. Behind you, thirty mushrooms turned slowly to watch."},
"night-sea":{"arrive":"Warm black water, lanterns swaying on your boat, and stars below as well as above. Far down, one of the stars is not moving.","beats":[{"day":30,"text":"The light at the bottom is bigger tonight. The fish here swim with their eyes shut, and somehow never bump into anything.","options":[{"t":"Lean over for a closer look","ok":false,"r":"It is lovely, and warm on your face. It seems to grow while you watch."},{"t":"Fish with your eyes shut","ok":true,"r":"You catch three fish by feel. Far below, the light stays put."},{"t":"Shine a lantern down at it","ok":false,"r":"Far below, something brightens, as if to answer."}]},{"day":140,"text":"Under the bench, a note in an old sailor's hand: Look up, never down. It looks back. The light below is bigger than the boat now.","options":[{"t":"Draw a map of the glow","ok":false,"r":"You stare all night to get it right. By morning it is closer."},{"t":"Peek over the side, once","ok":false,"r":"It is very close now, and it has noticed you."},{"t":"Lie back and count stars","ok":true,"r":"You count the stars above until dawn. Below, the glow dims a little."}]},{"day":290,"text":"Tonight the whole sea glows from underneath. Your shadow points up at the sky. Then, very slowly, the light blinks.","options":[{"t":"Tie a scarf over your eyes","ok":true,"r":"You sit blind till morning, humming. The glow sinks back, sulking."},{"t":"Look down to see what blinked","ok":false,"r":"Something huge looks back up at you. The boat rocks gently upward."},{"t":"Wave at it, to be friendly","ok":false,"r":"The light rises, delighted. The water turns warm under your hand."}]}],"alt":"You never looked down, not once. The light rose all year, then sank back, tired of waiting, and you sailed on under the real stars."},
"double-well":{"arrive":"A quiet meadow, a warm cottage, and a well with a bucket on a rope. You drop in an apple, and two come back up.","beats":[{"day":30,"text":"Two apples, two pears, two of everything. Scratched on the rim: mind yourself. Your hat blows off and lands on the dark water far below.","options":[{"t":"Lean in and reach for it","ok":false,"r":"Your fingers brush the water. Down below, another hand reaches up."},{"t":"Kneel on the rim and peer in","ok":false,"r":"Your face looks up from the water. It stays there after you pull back."},{"t":"Lower the bucket for it","ok":true,"r":"Up come two hats, both yours. You wear one and give one to the scarecrow."}]},{"day":150,"text":"An old notice is nailed to the well post: Use the bucket only. Keep both feet on the grass. Tonight you hear humming down there.","options":[{"t":"Fetch water and walk away","ok":true,"r":"The humming stops when you leave. Two full buckets, as always."},{"t":"Shout down, who's there?","ok":false,"r":"Your own voice answers, a little too quickly."},{"t":"Sit on the rim to listen","ok":false,"r":"The humming climbs closer to the top. You hop down, cold all over."}]},{"day":300,"text":"The old rope snaps and the bucket falls. Silence. Then, from far down, comes the sound of someone climbing, two by two.","options":[{"t":"Look down to see who it is","ok":false,"r":"Two faces look up. Both of them are yours, and both are smiling."},{"t":"Lower a new rope to help","ok":false,"r":"Something grabs hold at once. You lean to see, and it sees you."},{"t":"Slide the lid on, eyes up","ok":true,"r":"You push the heavy lid shut, eyes on the sky. The climbing stops."}]}],"alt":"You never leaned over. The well gave you two of everything all year, but only ever one of you. Some nights it still calls your name, twice."},
"empty-zoo":{"arrive":"Warm lamps along the paths, three hundred cages with every door open, and not one animal. The map by the gate is very old.","beats":[{"day":40,"text":"Each morning one more cage door has closed by itself, with a new sign: Lions. Parrots. An open cage nearby has a lovely soft bed.","options":[{"t":"Nap on a bench by the path","ok":true,"r":"The lamps hum. In the night a far door closes. Not near you."},{"t":"Nap in the soft cage","ok":false,"r":"You wake to a click. The door is still open, but only just."},{"t":"Step inside to read its sign","ok":false,"r":"The sign is blank. The door creaks a little behind you."}]},{"day":180,"text":"Only forty cages are still open, all at the far end past the pond, signs blank. Cutting past them is the shortest way to the cafe.","options":[{"t":"Cut through, quickly","ok":false,"r":"Every blank sign seems to turn as you pass. One door swings, very slightly."},{"t":"Take the long way round","ok":true,"r":"Your tea is cold when you arrive, but the blank cages stay far behind."}]},{"day":340,"text":"Three cages left open. This morning one has a fresh sign: Humans. Inside is a warm lamp, your favourite chair, and a cup of tea.","options":[{"t":"Sit, just for one cup","ok":false,"r":"The tea is perfect. The door eases shut a little while you sip."},{"t":"Take down the sign","ok":false,"r":"Behind it is another sign, with your name on it."},{"t":"Walk to the exit gate","ok":true,"r":"The path to the gate is long and cold. You do not look back."}]}],"alt":"You kept well clear of the last cages. On Friday the final door closed softly on nobody, and the front gates swung open for you."},
"scarecrow":{"arrive":"Golden corn to the edge of the world, a farmhouse, and a moon that never sets. In every field stands one scarecrow, arms out.","beats":[{"day":40,"text":"The crows here always face the scarecrows, and leave by walking backwards. One field over, a scarecrow stands where there was none.","options":[{"t":"Turn and hurry home","ok":false,"r":"Behind you the corn rustles. Next morning it is one field nearer."},{"t":"Walk home backwards too","ok":true,"r":"It takes ages and you trip once. The scarecrow stays exactly where it was."},{"t":"Pick corn and ignore it","ok":false,"r":"You work with your back to it all day. At dusk it is at the field's edge."}]},{"day":160,"text":"Two scarecrows in the next field now, both facing the house. It's washing day, and the line makes you stand with your back to them.","options":[{"t":"Move the line to face them","ok":true,"r":"You peg sheets with them in full view. They do not move an inch."},{"t":"Peg it all out really fast","ok":false,"r":"When you turn round, one of them is a whole row closer."},{"t":"Hang a mirror by the line","ok":true,"r":"In the mirror they stay still while you peg. A crow nods at you."}]},{"day":330,"text":"This morning one stands in your garden, facing your window. You need logs from the shed, round behind the house.","options":[{"t":"Draw the curtains","ok":false,"r":"Behind the cloth, something taps softly on the glass."},{"t":"Run for the shed","ok":false,"r":"When you get back, its shadow is lying across the porch."},{"t":"Edge there, eyes on it","ok":true,"r":"Step by step, eyes on its sack face. It does not move while you watch."}]}],"alt":"You never turned your back, not once in a year. On the last morning it was still in the garden, facing you, very patiently."},
"endless-mall":{"arrive":"Soft music, warm lights, and everything free. Every shop has a metal shutter, and a little clock above it, set to nine.","beats":[{"day":30,"text":"Five to nine. Shoppers drift into the stores and the shutters start to hum. You're in the food court, halfway through a free milkshake.","options":[{"t":"Finish the milkshake first","ok":false,"r":"The music stops. You dive under a shutter with one second to spare."},{"t":"Duck into the nearest shop","ok":true,"r":"The shutter comes down behind you. Outside, something squeaks past on soft wheels."},{"t":"Wait on a bench","ok":false,"r":"Something with a mop pauses by your bench, then rolls on. Just."}]},{"day":150,"text":"The best sale tonight is on the top floor, a long walk from any open shop. It's ten to nine, and the music is on its last song.","options":[{"t":"Ride the escalator up","ok":false,"r":"It is so slow. The song ends as you reach the top. You barely make it."},{"t":"Shop downstairs, by a door","ok":true,"r":"At nine you step inside with time to spare. The sale can wait."},{"t":"Run up for a quick look","ok":false,"r":"The music stops halfway up. You squeeze under a shutter, breathless."}]},{"day":300,"text":"The music stops early tonight, at eight. Ten seconds. The shop beside you has its shutter half down. The escalator is right there.","options":[{"t":"Run for the escalator","ok":false,"r":"It is very slow tonight. Something with a broom waits at the bottom."},{"t":"Freeze and look tidy","ok":false,"r":"A long soft mop reaches out to check if you are mess."},{"t":"Roll under the shutter","ok":true,"r":"You slide in as it clicks shut. Outside, the cleaners hum and sweep."}]}],"alt":"Every night the music stopped, and every night you were already inside a shop. The cleaners swept past your shutter all year, humming."},
"pumpkin-patch":{"arrive":"Pumpkins to the horizon, a warm farmhouse, and fresh pie on the sill. At midnight, every pumpkin glows and turns toward you.","beats":[{"day":40,"text":"A note in the pie tin: Enjoy the pie. Never keep a tally. Out in the patch, one pumpkin's carved nose looks a lot like yours.","options":[{"t":"Count the ones by the gate","ok":false,"r":"Forty-one. You are sure it was forty last night. The new one grins."},{"t":"Eat pie and enjoy the glow","ok":true,"r":"Warm crust, warm light. The pumpkins glow softly, and nobody counts."}]},{"day":170,"text":"Midnight. More of the faces look like you now, you're nearly sure of it. The urge to count them is very strong.","options":[{"t":"Count only the ones like you","ok":false,"r":"Seven. Then eight. The eighth one blinks."},{"t":"Draw the curtains and read","ok":true,"r":"You read until the glow fades. Outside, nothing grows any closer."},{"t":"Chalk a number on each","ok":false,"r":"You run out of chalk before pumpkins. One you missed is grinning."}]},{"day":330,"text":"Last nights of harvest. The whole patch wears your face now, smiling. All except one by the door, which is somehow new.","options":[{"t":"Bake a pie and stay in","ok":true,"r":"The kitchen smells of cinnamon. Outside, a thousand smiles wait for nothing."},{"t":"Check if it's one more","ok":false,"r":"You count, to be sure. There is one more than there should be."},{"t":"Roll the new one away","ok":false,"r":"It is heavy and warm. When you look back, there are two by the door."}]}],"alt":"You never counted them. On the last night they all glowed and smiled at your window, and you drew the curtains and had more pie."},
"drive-in":{"arrive":"A giant screen under the stars, your own little car, and a bucket of free popcorn. Tonight's film begins, and the first shot is your car.","beats":[{"day":30,"text":"Tonight's film shows you tomorrow, spilling jam at breakfast. A sign by the gate says: Kindly leave before the end. Nobody does.","options":[{"t":"Stay for the credits","ok":false,"r":"The last scene is you, watching the credits. Your popcorn goes cold."},{"t":"Leave before the last scene","ok":true,"r":"You drive off as the music swells. Tomorrow surprises you, nicely."},{"t":"Look for the projectionist","ok":false,"r":"The booth is empty. The film runs on, and the ending finds you anyway."}]},{"day":160,"text":"The films get a minute shorter every week. Tonight's ends right here, with you, at this screen. The ending is ten minutes away.","options":[{"t":"Fetch more popcorn first","ok":false,"r":"When you get back, the last scene is already playing."},{"t":"Stay to see what happens","ok":false,"r":"You see yourself sitting here, seeing yourself. It is very quiet."},{"t":"Drive off before it ends","ok":true,"r":"Your headlights sweep the field. The screen flickers, cross with you."}]},{"day":330,"text":"Tonight's film is only five minutes long. On the poster, there is no tomorrow after it. The popcorn is warm, the seat is soft.","options":[{"t":"Leave before the lights dim","ok":true,"r":"You drive into the dark before the titles. Behind you the screen lights up, for nobody."},{"t":"Watch just the first minute","ok":false,"r":"One minute becomes five. You cannot look away from the ending."},{"t":"Settle in with the popcorn","ok":false,"r":"The film is short and very still. The popcorn stays warm all night."}]}],"alt":"On the night of the five-minute film, you drove away before the opening titles. Behind you, it ended without you, and the screen went white."},
"endless-library":{"arrive":"Soft lamps, deep chairs, and books to the ceiling and beyond. A tall librarian looks up from her desk and lays one finger on her lips.","beats":[{"day":30,"text":"A man two tables away whispers: excuse me? By morning he is gone. On the new books shelf sits a book with his face on the cover.","options":[{"t":"Ask the librarian about him","ok":false,"r":"She looks at you for a long time. A blank book appears on a shelf."},{"t":"Whisper his name to yourself","ok":false,"r":"The lamp flickers. Somewhere, a pen begins to write."},{"t":"Write her a note instead","ok":true,"r":"She reads it and nods, pleased. She writes back one word: Good."}]},{"day":170,"text":"You find a terribly funny book. A laugh is building in your chest. The librarian is three aisles away, but she hears everything.","options":[{"t":"Let out one tiny chuckle","ok":false,"r":"Her head turns at once. A shelf nearby quietly makes room."},{"t":"Close it and breathe slowly","ok":true,"r":"The laugh melts into a smile. The librarian walks past, silent as snow."},{"t":"Read on, lips pressed tight","ok":false,"r":"The laugh escapes as a snort. Every page in the library rustles."}]},{"day":330,"text":"You've caught a cold, and your nose tickles all day. Eleven months of silence, and the librarian has begun to watch you very closely.","options":[{"t":"Hold your breath and hope","ok":false,"r":"It doesn't pass. Achoo. The whole library goes still."},{"t":"Say sorry to her in advance","ok":false,"r":"Two words. Behind her desk, her pen begins to write."},{"t":"Pinch your nose in a hanky","ok":true,"r":"The sneeze shrinks to nothing. The librarian blinks, almost impressed."}]}],"alt":"You kept quiet for twelve whole months, even through a cold. The librarian stamped your card and smiled, and the shelf stayed one book short."},
"teddy-bear-hills":{"arrive":"Soft green hills, honey on tap, and giant teddy bears waving from every slope. Far off, one bear sits very still, holding something.","beats":[{"day":30,"text":"A big bear scoops you up for a hug. It's lovely. You notice the bears let go much sooner when people keep their arms by their sides.","options":[{"t":"Hug the bear back","ok":false,"r":"It squeezes harder, delighted. It takes all afternoon to wriggle free."},{"t":"Keep your arms by your sides","ok":true,"r":"The bear squeezes, sighs happily, and sets you down. Fair enough."},{"t":"Pat its back politely","ok":false,"r":"It takes that as a yes. You miss lunch."}]},{"day":160,"text":"The hugs last longer now. On the far hill the still bear hums, a traveller's hat poking out of its arms. A cub holds its arms up to you.","options":[{"t":"Give the cub some honey","ok":true,"r":"It forgets the hug at once and sits down to eat, beaming."},{"t":"Hug the little one, once","ok":false,"r":"Tiny, but very strong. Its mother joins in. The afternoon disappears."},{"t":"Let it hug you, arms down","ok":true,"r":"It clings to your knees a while, then toddles off, sleepy."}]},{"day":300,"text":"Your birthday. Every bear on the hills lines up to hug you, one after another. The first is the biggest of them all, eyes shining.","options":[{"t":"Hug them all, it's your day","ok":false,"r":"It is the warmest hug ever. The queue waits patiently, for a long time."},{"t":"Hug just the big one back","ok":false,"r":"It hums and holds on. The sun sets, and it is still holding on."},{"t":"Stand still and smile","ok":true,"r":"One by one they squeeze and set you down. You are dizzy, sticky and free."}]}],"alt":"The bears hugged you all year, and you never once hugged back. Every hug ended, eventually. You left very sticky, and very loved."},
"night-market":{"arrive":"Paper lanterns, steaming noodles, and stalls that never close. No one here carries money. Nobody seems to need any.","beats":[{"day":30,"text":"The noodle man hands you a bowl before you ask. He only arrived last week, he says, though his beard is long and white.","options":[{"t":"Thank him and tuck in","ok":false,"r":"Delicious. That night, you find your very first grey hair."},{"t":"Ask what it costs first","ok":true,"r":"He looks surprised. One day, he says. You hand the bowl back, politely."},{"t":"Eat half, save the rest","ok":false,"r":"Half a bowl still costs a whole day. You feel it in your knees."}]},{"day":150,"text":"A stall has warm winter coats, no price tags. The girl who bought one yesterday looks a year older today, and very puzzled.","options":[{"t":"Try one on, just to see","ok":false,"r":"It fits perfectly. The seller nods. It is yours now, and so is the bill."},{"t":"Ask the seller the price","ok":true,"r":"One day, she says. You decide to knit your own instead."},{"t":"Pick the plainest coat","ok":false,"r":"Every coat here costs the same. You feel the price settle in your bones."}]},{"day":300,"text":"You're hungry and tired. A stall offers free samples, and a sign says: No charge. People grab handfuls without asking.","options":[{"t":"Grab a handful","ok":false,"r":"Delicious. Your face in a puddle looks unfamiliar, and older."},{"t":"Take one small bite","ok":false,"r":"One bite, one day. You can feel it go."},{"t":"Ask the price anyway","ok":true,"r":"The seller sighs. Free, but one day a bite. You walk on, hungry but whole."}]}],"alt":"You asked every price, and paid almost none. You cooked your own rice by lantern light, and left the market just a year older, no more."},
"playground":{"arrive":"Swings at sunset, a slide, and a clubhouse with your name on the door. Close by, children are laughing. You can't see any of them.","beats":[{"day":30,"text":"A red ball rolls out of nowhere and stops at your feet. The laughing pauses, waiting. Someone has scratched one word on the slide: don't.","options":[{"t":"Kick it back to them","ok":false,"r":"The laughing comes back, closer. Something runs past, just out of sight."},{"t":"Leave it, go to the swings","ok":true,"r":"The ball sits there till dark. The laughing drifts off somewhere else."},{"t":"Roll it back gently","ok":false,"r":"Something catches it. Little footsteps patter all around you."}]},{"day":160,"text":"The ball comes every evening now, and the laughing gets closer. Tonight a voice calls from the clubhouse roof: throw it, throw it!","options":[{"t":"Bounce it, just once","ok":false,"r":"It bounces off into the dusk. Somebody giggles: almost!"},{"t":"Toss it up onto the roof","ok":false,"r":"It never comes down. The laughing jumps much closer."},{"t":"Tuck it in a cupboard","ok":true,"r":"The voice sulks. By morning the cupboard is empty, and quiet."}]},{"day":300,"text":"The ball rolls out again. Beside it, letters appear slowly in the sand: your turn soon. The laughing is right behind you.","options":[{"t":"Walk into the clubhouse","ok":true,"r":"You lock the door and read till morning. The ball waits, then rolls away."},{"t":"Throw it far away","ok":false,"r":"It goes far. Then it comes back, faster, and the laughing stops."},{"t":"Ask whose turn it is","ok":false,"r":"Silence. Then a small voice: well, it was mine."}]}],"alt":"Every evening the red ball rolled out, and every evening you let it lie. On the last night the laughing faded, and someone sighed: next year."},
"observatory":{"arrive":"Above the clouds, a tiny observatory, and the clearest sky you've ever seen. One star, low in the east, is brighter than the rest.","beats":[{"day":40,"text":"Through the telescope, the bright star is square and yellow, like a lit window. The old logbook ends mid-sentence: it waved, so I waved back, and","options":[{"t":"Note it in the logbook","ok":true,"r":"You add a line under it: did not wave. The window flickers, puzzled."},{"t":"Wave, to be friendly","ok":false,"r":"The shape stops. It leans closer to its side of the glass."},{"t":"Signal with your torch","ok":false,"r":"The window blinks back. Twice."}]},{"day":170,"text":"The shape is clearly a person now, and it waves at you through the telescope. The logbook says: it is lonely. It is patient. Don't.","options":[{"t":"Wave back, just a little","ok":false,"r":"It waves harder. By morning the window is twice the size."},{"t":"Turn the telescope away","ok":true,"r":"You study a different star all night. The window dims, disappointed."},{"t":"Smile and nod back","ok":false,"r":"It nods too. The window is bigger now, and a little closer."}]},{"day":320,"text":"The window fills half the sky. The person in it holds up a sign: please. Your hand is already halfway up, out of habit.","options":[{"t":"Wave goodbye to it","ok":false,"r":"Goodbye is still a wave. The window opens, just a little."},{"t":"Put your hands in pockets","ok":true,"r":"You keep your hands warm and still. The window slowly draws away."},{"t":"Close the dome and sleep","ok":true,"r":"The dome rolls shut. Overhead, something taps once, then leaves."}]}],"alt":"Someone in the window waved every night, and you never waved back. By winter it dimmed, drifted off, and became a star again."},
"sunken-city":{"arrive":"Warm lamps glow under the water, every door is unlocked, and you can breathe just fine. In the square, stone statues ring a fountain.","beats":[{"day":30,"text":"One more statue this morning. Chalked on a doorway: in the square, mind your feet. The little fish all cross it with their eyes down.","options":[{"t":"Swim round to see its face","ok":false,"r":"It looks like someone very surprised. Your fingers feel stiff and cold."},{"t":"Cross watching your feet","ok":true,"r":"You count tiles all the way across. The statues stay statues."},{"t":"Peek at it in a shop window","ok":false,"r":"In the glass, its eyes meet yours. Your toes go numb for an hour."}]},{"day":160,"text":"Today's statue reaches out a stone hand, as if asking for help. Its face is tipped toward you, very close. You keep your eyes on its shoes.","options":[{"t":"Look up to see who it is","ok":false,"r":"Its eyes are kind, and very still. Your knees creak like stone."},{"t":"Shut your eyes, back away","ok":true,"r":"You back off blind till you bump a lamp post. Safe, a little bruised."},{"t":"Drop your hat over its face","ok":true,"r":"Only then do you look. It is just a statue, hiding under your hat."}]},{"day":310,"text":"This morning's statue wears your backpack. It faces your front door instead of the fountain. You must walk right past it to get out.","options":[{"t":"Look at it, just to know","ok":false,"r":"It has your face. Your fingers begin to stiffen."},{"t":"Take your backpack back","ok":false,"r":"To reach the straps, you have to look up. Its eyes are open."},{"t":"Pass it, eyes on the floor","ok":true,"r":"You see only its stone shoes. They are your shoes. You keep walking."}]}],"alt":"You never once looked at a stone face. The square kept its statues, you kept your smile, and you swam home under the warm lamps."},
"kaiju-bones":{"arrive":"Your cabin sits snug inside giant mossy ribs, fireflies drifting between them. The ribs creak softly, like a ship. Or like breathing.","beats":[{"day":40,"text":"A tail bone has moved back into place overnight. You notice the bones only shift after noisy days, and the fireflies dim when you're loud.","options":[{"t":"Bang a pot to test it","ok":false,"r":"The ribs shiver. Somewhere far off, a claw twitches."},{"t":"Gather twigs quietly","ok":true,"r":"A small, hushed fire. The bones stay exactly where they were."},{"t":"Chop wood at dawn anyway","ok":false,"r":"Thunk, thunk. By night, a leg bone has clicked into place."}]},{"day":180,"text":"The legs are back. A storm is coming, and your cabin door keeps slamming in the wind. The fireflies huddle, flickering.","options":[{"t":"Nail it shut, quickly","ok":false,"r":"Bang, bang, bang. Something deep below grunts in its sleep."},{"t":"Let it slam, it's only wind","ok":false,"r":"It slams all night. By morning the spine has shifted, just a little."},{"t":"Wedge it with a soft sock","ok":true,"r":"The door sighs shut. The storm passes, and the bones sleep on."}]},{"day":320,"text":"Only the skull is left. Tonight you hear it click into place. Then, very slowly, a heartbeat, deep under the cabin floor.","options":[{"t":"Tiptoe out between the ribs","ok":true,"r":"You slip out into the dark, barefoot. Behind you, the heartbeat stays slow."},{"t":"Shout to see if it's awake","ok":false,"r":"The heartbeat quickens. The floor tilts, just slightly."},{"t":"Pack everything and run","ok":false,"r":"Pots clatter. An eye the size of your cabin opens, sleepily."}]}],"alt":"You tiptoed all year and never woke it. In December you crept out between the ribs. Behind you, something huge sighed and rolled over."},
"video-store":{"arrive":"A cosy video store, soft lamps, a couch, and a shelf of tapes with dates on them. The first tape is labelled with your birthday.","beats":[{"day":40,"text":"Each tape is one day of your life, in order. Tonight is your tenth birthday. Behind the counter, a tape marked tomorrow sits alone, behind a little rope.","options":[{"t":"Peek at tomorrow's tape","ok":false,"r":"Ten seconds of you on this couch, and a shape behind you you hadn't noticed."},{"t":"Watch your tenth birthday","ok":true,"r":"Cake, candles, a wobbly bike. You fall asleep smiling on the couch."}]},{"day":200,"text":"The tapes are nearly caught up: last week, then yesterday. The couch has two dents in it now. The newest tape says: tomorrow.","options":[{"t":"Rewatch yesterday's tape","ok":true,"r":"You see yourself making tea. Nothing new. You sleep well."},{"t":"Play tomorrow's, just to see","ok":false,"r":"On screen, someone sits down beside you. You look. Nobody is there."},{"t":"Take tomorrow's up to bed","ok":false,"r":"It whirs by itself all night. Downstairs, the couch creaks."}]},{"day":330,"text":"Only one tape left: tomorrow. The player hums, ready. In the dark screen you can see someone standing right behind you.","options":[{"t":"Press play, quickly","ok":false,"r":"The screen shows tomorrow: this couch, and nobody on it."},{"t":"Put it back on the shelf","ok":true,"r":"You slide it back, unwatched. In the dark screen, the figure is gone."},{"t":"Unplug the player and leave","ok":true,"r":"Silence. You walk out into the morning, and nobody films it."}]}],"alt":"You never played tomorrow's tape. You left it on the shelf, unwatched, and walked out into a tomorrow nobody had filmed."},
"pawn-shop":{"arrive":"A cosy little shop, a kettle always on, and a kind old shopkeeper. Glowing jars line every shelf, each one numbered.","beats":[{"day":30,"text":"You need a blanket. He smiles: no money, just one small memory, your first ice cream. The last customer left humming, eyes a bit blank.","options":[{"t":"Sell just that one","ok":false,"r":"A new jar glows pink. You can't remember what ice cream tastes like."},{"t":"Sew one from old coats","ok":true,"r":"Lumpy, but warm. The shopkeeper looks disappointed, kindly."},{"t":"Offer to sweep the shop","ok":true,"r":"Only memories, dear, he says gently. You stay cold, but whole."}]},{"day":160,"text":"Winter is coming. He offers a whole cart of firewood for one small memory: a rainy Tuesday you've surely forgotten anyway.","options":[{"t":"Bargain for half a cart","ok":false,"r":"Half a memory is still a memory. You forget how rain smells."},{"t":"Chop wood in the forest","ok":true,"r":"Your arms ache, but the stack grows. Every log is your own."},{"t":"Sell the rainy Tuesday","ok":false,"r":"The jar glows grey. Now and then you feel a Tuesday-shaped gap."}]},{"day":320,"text":"He offers to cure your cough for one memory of home. On the shelf behind him, a jar with your name on it sits waiting, empty.","options":[{"t":"Trade, just this once","ok":false,"r":"Your jar gets its first glow. Home goes a little blurry."},{"t":"Ask to hold your jar","ok":false,"r":"He hands it over. It is warm, and it feels like it wants filling."},{"t":"Brew honey tea yourself","ok":true,"r":"The cough lingers, then fades. Home stays sharp and bright in your head."}]}],"alt":"You never sold a memory, not even a small one. You chopped your own wood, and the jar with your name stayed empty, and clear."},
"sunbeam-orchard":{"arrive":"A warm hill, apple trees humming with bees, a quilt on the bed. Every apple you pick grows back by morning, with a tiny ribbon tied on.","beats":[{"day":30,"text":"Nobody's ever around, but every regrown apple wears a ribbon. Your neighbour always hangs a little jar of honey on each tree she picks from.","options":[{"t":"Tie a ribbon on a branch","ok":true,"r":"Next morning, a bigger ribbon is tied beside yours, in a neat bow."},{"t":"Pick, and get on with the day","ok":false,"r":"The apple tastes fine. The next one grows back a little smaller."},{"t":"Stay up to catch who ties them","ok":false,"r":"Nobody comes while you watch. The morning apples have no ribbons."}]},{"day":160,"text":"A storm knocks down half the apples. In the morning the fallen ones are stacked by your door, each one wrapped in ribbon.","options":[{"t":"Store them away, quickly","ok":false,"r":"They keep well, but the next ribbons are tied a little loosely."},{"t":"Pin a note to the tree","ok":true,"r":"The note is gone by noon. A tiny drawing of a smile is left in its place."},{"t":"Leave out a slice of pie","ok":true,"r":"The plate is licked clean by morning, with a ribbon on the fork."}]},{"day":300,"text":"Your birthday. You wake to find every tree on the hill tied with ribbons, and a basket of golden apples on your step.","options":[{"t":"Eat them all before lunch","ok":false,"r":"Delicious. Tomorrow, the ribbons on the trees look faded."},{"t":"Search the hill for the giver","ok":false,"r":"You search till dark and find nobody. The basket on your step is empty."},{"t":"Call thank you over the hill","ok":true,"r":"The whole orchard rustles. A golden ribbon flutters down onto your hat."}]}],"alt":"Some apples you took without a word. The ribbons came back thinner, some mornings not at all. Still, the orchard fed you all year."},
"teacup-sea":{"arrive":"Your boat is a teacup, the sea is warm and calm, and the air smells faintly of honey. A huge china handle rises over the horizon.","beats":[{"day":30,"text":"Evening. The tide pours into the giant teacup and the sea starts to steam. The fish go sleepy and drift up. Your oar is still in the water.","options":[{"t":"Row on through the steam","ok":false,"r":"Little whirlpools spin off your oar. The fish wake up, cross."},{"t":"Lift the oar and wait","ok":true,"r":"The sea settles, sweet and still. A sleepy fish flops into your boat."},{"t":"Swish it to feel the warmth","ok":false,"r":"The water swirls. The whole sea sloshes, and so does your stomach."}]},{"day":150,"text":"A turtle with a shell like a sugar lump bumps your boat, wanting to play. Last time you towed it about, the sea spun for an hour.","options":[{"t":"Let it nap by the boat","ok":true,"r":"It snores softly, steam curling off its shell. The sea stays smooth."},{"t":"Tow it round in circles","ok":false,"r":"Round and round. The whole sea begins to swirl, and so does your head."},{"t":"Offer it a biscuit","ok":true,"r":"It dunks the biscuit very politely, and drifts off happy."}]},{"day":300,"text":"Your net is snagged far below. The quickest fix is to swing the boat round and round until it pulls free. The tea hour is close.","options":[{"t":"Dive in to free it","ok":false,"r":"Splash. Rings of ripples spread out. The steam wobbles, annoyed."},{"t":"Swing round and tug it free","ok":false,"r":"The sea spins like a whirlpool. Your teacup is dizzy for a week."},{"t":"Wait for the hush, then lift","ok":true,"r":"The steam rises, the sea goes still, and the net slides up full of fish."}]}],"alt":"Now and then you stirred the sea, and it spun until you were seasick. Still, the fish forgave you, mostly, and the honey tide came every night."},
"sleeping-giants":{"arrive":"Mossy green hills, a snug cabin, and a valley so quiet you can hear the hills breathe. Slowly. In, and out.","beats":[{"day":30,"text":"Your garden has been rearranged in the night: carrots in the birdbath, the fence upside down. The hill out back has a new shape, and it snores.","options":[{"t":"Whisper thanks to the hill","ok":true,"r":"The snoring turns to a soft hum. The carrots do very well in the birdbath."},{"t":"Shout to find out who did it","ok":false,"r":"The ground rumbles. The hill rolls over again and squashes your shed a bit."},{"t":"Tidy up, humming softly","ok":true,"r":"You hum under your breath as you work. The hill sleeps on, smiling."}]},{"day":150,"text":"A friend visits and wants to hear the famous valley echo. Look closely and every hill has a soft, mossy ear.","options":[{"t":"Shout hello across the valley","ok":false,"r":"Hello, hello. A hill grumbles and rolls, and your friend's tent ends up in a tree."},{"t":"Teach them to whisper-sing","ok":true,"r":"Your tiny song drifts across the valley. The hills sigh, content."},{"t":"Clap as loud as you can","ok":false,"r":"A hill twitches like a dreaming dog. Your well is on the roof now."}]},{"day":300,"text":"A hill rolls over at midnight. Your bed ends up outside under the stars, with the hill's huge sleeping face right beside you.","options":[{"t":"Yell for it to move over","ok":false,"r":"It groans and rolls the other way. Your roof is in the pond now."},{"t":"Sleep out under the stars","ok":true,"r":"You drift off by its warm mossy cheek. Best night's sleep of the year."},{"t":"Whisper it a lullaby","ok":true,"r":"Its breathing slows. By morning your bed is back inside, mostly."}]}],"alt":"Some days you forgot and shouted. The hills grumbled and rolled twice as often, and your garden spent most of the year upside down."},
"star-mailbox":{"arrive":"A hilltop cabin, a telescope, and a sky full of stars. At midnight something warm and glowing drops into your mailbox with a soft clink.","beats":[{"day":30,"text":"Inside the star is a tiny note: I wish my cat would come home. Signed by a girl far away, who has given up. The star is still warm.","options":[{"t":"Keep it on your shelf","ok":false,"r":"It glows on the shelf all night, a little dimmer by morning."},{"t":"Write back, then send it on","ok":true,"r":"You write: don't give up. You toss it up, and it streaks off, brighter."},{"t":"Make a wish on it yourself","ok":false,"r":"Nothing happens. The note inside curls up, sadly."}]},{"day":160,"text":"Tonight's star holds a wish for a red bicycle. Your neighbour says the stars she answered came back as thank-you notes in the frost.","options":[{"t":"Draw a bicycle, send it off","ok":true,"r":"Off it goes, sparkling. A week later a tiny bell rings, far away."},{"t":"Save it in a jar for later","ok":false,"r":"In the jar it flickers, waiting. You forget about it for months."},{"t":"Send back a funny poem","ok":true,"r":"The star seems to giggle and zips off. The sky twinkles for an hour."}]},{"day":300,"text":"A big, heavy star tonight, nearly cold. The wish inside says only: I wish someone would write back. It isn't signed.","options":[{"t":"Leave it, it's too sad","ok":false,"r":"It cools in the mailbox overnight, quietly."},{"t":"Keep it for yourself","ok":false,"r":"It sits on your shelf, a little grey, still waiting for a letter."},{"t":"Write a long, kind letter","ok":true,"r":"It warms in your hands as you write, then leaves like a firework."}]}],"alt":"Some wishes you kept in a drawer instead of answering. They glowed there, a bit sadly, all year. Still, the sky kept sending more."},
"weather-shop":{"arrive":"A tiny hilltop shop, shelves of little jars, each holding a day of weather. One on the top shelf is grey, labelled: not the grey one.","beats":[{"day":30,"text":"A dull day. You open a jar marked sunny and the kitchen fills with warm light. Up top, the grey jar rattles, as if it wants a turn.","options":[{"t":"Shake the grey jar to listen","ok":false,"r":"Something swirls inside. A snowflake slips out under the lid."},{"t":"Open another sunny one","ok":true,"r":"Another golden day. The grey jar goes still, sulking."},{"t":"Peek under its lid","ok":false,"r":"A cold wind whistles out. Frost on the windows for two days."}]},{"day":150,"text":"A customer wants snow for her child's birthday. The only snow jars left sit on the top shelf, right beside the grey one.","options":[{"t":"Give her the grey jar","ok":false,"r":"She opens it at home. It is still snowing there in June."},{"t":"Grab one quick, on tiptoe","ok":false,"r":"The shelf wobbles. The grey jar's lid shifts, and frost creeps out."},{"t":"Fetch the step stool","ok":true,"r":"You lift a snow jar down without a wobble. The grey one stays put."}]},{"day":200,"text":"Day two hundred. A muffled tapping comes from the grey jar, like knocking from inside. A tiny voice says: just for a minute.","options":[{"t":"Open it, just for a minute","ok":false,"r":"It snows in your kitchen for a week. You wear three coats."},{"t":"Open a calm jar instead","ok":true,"r":"A still, quiet day settles over the shop. The tapping stops."},{"t":"Loosen the lid a tiny bit","ok":false,"r":"A tiny bit is plenty. Snow pours out like flour."}]}],"alt":"You opened the grey jar more than once. The snow came, and kept coming, until the little shop on the hill was one soft white hump."},
"echo-canyon":{"arrive":"A red canyon at sunrise, a cosy ledge, and the best view for miles. You call good morning, and the canyon says nothing. Yet.","beats":[{"day":20,"text":"Today the canyon calls out good morning in your voice, a whole day late. When the echo booms, loose stones rattle down the cliff.","options":[{"t":"Shout YAHOO, just for fun","ok":false,"r":"Tomorrow a huge YAHOO wakes you at dawn and sends pebbles bouncing."},{"t":"Choose your words, speak soft","ok":true,"r":"Tomorrow the canyon says them back gently, and nothing falls."},{"t":"Sing loudly while you cook","ok":false,"r":"Next day it sings back off-key, and a stone hops past your boot."}]},{"day":150,"text":"A hawk steals your sandwich and you nearly yell. Tomorrow you'll be on the narrow cliff path, when the canyon shouts it back.","options":[{"t":"Shoo it with a silent wave","ok":true,"r":"The hawk flaps off. Tomorrow the cliff path is calm and quiet."},{"t":"Shout: get lost!","ok":false,"r":"Next day on the path, GET LOST booms out. You cling to the rock."},{"t":"Shout: come back here!","ok":false,"r":"Next day a voice yells COME BACK, and you nearly turn on the narrow path."}]},{"day":300,"text":"Tonight an echo arrives early, in your own worried voice: don't go down! You were planning to hike down to the river at dawn.","options":[{"t":"Go anyway, it's just an echo","ok":false,"r":"Halfway down, stones rattle past. You scramble back up, shaking."},{"t":"Stay up on the ledge","ok":true,"r":"At dawn a rockslide rumbles down the river path. You sip tea, far above."},{"t":"Shout back: why not?","ok":false,"r":"WHY NOT rolls round the cliffs all night. Gravel patters on your roof."}]}],"alt":"You shouted without thinking, again and again. One day the canyon sent it all back at once. By evening the ledge was empty, and the echo said sorry."},
"hundred-floors":{"arrive":"A hundred floors, a warm lobby, and a lift that plays gentle jazz. The stairwell is long and echoey, and your flat is on floor ninety.","beats":[{"day":30,"text":"Ninety floors is a long climb. The lift dings invitingly. A neighbour with very strong legs says she hasn't used it in years. She won't say why.","options":[{"t":"Ride the lift, just today","ok":false,"r":"Smooth jazz. For a moment the numbers go past ninety, then come back."},{"t":"Climb the stairs","ok":true,"r":"Ninety floors. Your legs burn, but you sleep like a log."},{"t":"Take the lift halfway","ok":false,"r":"Floor forty-five takes oddly long to arrive. The music skips."}]},{"day":160,"text":"Late at night, a button with no number glows on the lift panel: 101. You're carrying heavy shopping, and the stairwell is dark.","options":[{"t":"Press 90 and hold it down","ok":false,"r":"The lift reaches 90, then pauses, humming, as if deciding."},{"t":"Climb up a bag at a time","ok":true,"r":"Two long trips. Through the wall, you hear the jazz playing for nobody."},{"t":"Send the bags up alone","ok":false,"r":"They never reach ninety. The lift comes back empty, smelling of rain."}]},{"day":330,"text":"Last night the lift opened on your floor by itself and waited, jazz playing. Today you twisted your ankle, and the doctor is in the lobby.","options":[{"t":"Wait in the lift for help","ok":false,"r":"The doors slide shut while you wait. The jazz gets a little louder."},{"t":"Ride down, just this once","ok":false,"r":"The doors close gently. The numbers start to climb: 91, 92."},{"t":"Bump down the stairs seated","ok":true,"r":"Ninety floors, one bump at a time. It takes all day, and you laugh at the end."}]}],"alt":"You took the stairs every day, all ninety floors. On the last night the lift doors opened, played a little jazz for nobody, and closed."},
"whisper-grass":{"arrive":"Tall silver grass, a straw bed, and a warm breeze. The grass rustles all day, and if you listen, it sounds almost like words.","beats":[{"day":30,"text":"This morning the grass whispers: pass the salt. That's what you said at supper yesterday. A shepherd passing by has wool in his ears.","options":[{"t":"Say: yes, I did say that","ok":false,"r":"The grass goes still, listening. Then it whispers that back, delighted."},{"t":"Hum and go about your day","ok":true,"r":"Your humming drowns it out. The grass loses track of you."},{"t":"Ask what else it heard","ok":false,"r":"It tells you, word for word, in your own voice."}]},{"day":120,"text":"Now the grass whispers things you haven't said yet: I'm lonely. I'll stay. It sounds so like you. It waits for a reply.","options":[{"t":"Tell it that isn't true","ok":false,"r":"It whispers that back, in a voice more like yours than yours."},{"t":"Stuff wool in your ears","ok":true,"r":"The meadow goes soft and muffled. You sleep without a single whisper."},{"t":"Walk off without a word","ok":true,"r":"Your footsteps are the only reply. The whispers fade behind you."}]},{"day":300,"text":"Last night the grass whispered goodbye, in your voice. Tonight it whispers your name, over and over, gently, waiting for you to say: yes?","options":[{"t":"Say yes, just to stop it","ok":false,"r":"Yes, it whispers, and the whole meadow says it in your voice."},{"t":"Keep quiet till sunrise","ok":true,"r":"Your name rustles all night. At dawn the grass gives up, and just sways."},{"t":"Say goodbye before it does","ok":false,"r":"Goodbye, the grass agrees. Your own voice feels thinner."}]}],"alt":"You never answered the grass, not once. It whispered your words all year, and by spring it ran out of them, and only rustled."}};
